{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win","id":1522398,"title":"Should the Technocracy win?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-11T06:41:45-07:00","id":1522398,"title":"Should the Technocracy win?","content":"The title I chose is admittedly click-bait, so don't take it <i>too</i> seriously. But I <i>do</i> want to entertain the possibility that an eventual Technocratic victory in the next decade or so may not only be possible, but maybe even desirable. Bear with me\u2026<br /> <br /> I have been listening to the Audiobook version of <i>The Fourth Turning is Here</i>, which argues that there's a generational cycle of history, with each generation lasting roughly 20 to 25 years or so and having a distinct character that is a reaction to their parents' generation and to which their children will react. This cycle consists of four generations \u2014 currently a Prophet generation (the Boomers), a Nomad generation (Generation X), a Hero generation (the Millennials), and an Artist generation (tentatively called the Homelanders). This cycle drives and is driven by a two-stroke cycle of cycle of spiritual awakenings and civic crises which in their turns remake and reinvigorate the culture (the Awakenings) and the government (the Crises). It's a fascinating read. <br /> <br /> <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, first published in the 90s, is a product of Generation X, and bears our distinctive characteristics: a mixture of pessimism and advocacy for individuality. But according to the theory, we are now firmly in the <i>middle</i> of a Crisis, which shows every indication of being as consequential as the last three Crises: the Great Depression and World War II, the Civil War, and the Revolutionary War. Assuming that this cycle resolved successfully, we'll be living in a distinctly different world in ten years, as different from today as the post-WWII world was from the pre-WWII world, or post-Civil War America was from pre-Civil War America, or the newborn American Republic was from the British colonies that birthed it. And if the past cycles are any indication, the post-Crisis world ten years from now will completely invert the characteristics I described above: expect a more optimistic tone and a tendency to extoll the virtues of community, service, and cooperation over individuality. <br /> <br /> Which brings me to my click-baity title: if <b>Mage</b> is a game about collectivism vs. individuality, with the Technocracy representing the former and the Traditions representing the latter, then chances are that the post-Crisis audience for the game will be firmly on the side of the Technocracy; and if the game doesn't adapt, it may lose whatever relevance it has. So: <i>should</i> <b>Mage</b> (eventually) be remade to that a reformed Technocracy is ascendant, with the Traditions coming to terms with it and possibly even joining forces with it? Or should the game stick to its guns and take the (by then) unpopular position of declaring that the post-Crisis world's likely emphasis on civic-mindedness is fatally flawed, taking <b>MRev</b>'s \u201cThe Ascension War is over, and we lost\u201d attitude up a notch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T09:28:41-07:00","id":1522403,"title":"","content":"I agree that it's a fascinating thing to think about - the tone updates of [x]20 and furor over [x]5 have gotten me thinking about how much of the character of the WoD games is very distinctly a product of the 90s. They're all horror games that reflect the fears of a specific generation. In particular, the generation <i>before</i> mine, so many of the themes don't resonate for me like they did when adolescent-me was looking up to the young-adults of the time. Some of it is almost quaint, now. Don't have time for a full post but I would draw your attention to the &quot;The Rise of the Extraordinary Citizen&quot; sidebar on page 155 of M20:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages of all factions who expected to lead a sheeplike humanity toward their pasture of choice have been shaken by what the New World Order calls the rise of the extraordinary citizen: a revolution in capability, conviction, and belief among the Masses.<br /> <br /> Whereas the fashionable apathy of the 1990s suggests a stagnation of human potential, the literally explosive events at the turn of the new millennium spotlight the very opposite idea. Although certain elements of consumeristic society scarf down Happy Meals and junk culture, the combination of political unrest, technological savvy, mystic romanticism, and religious convictions ignite worldwide upheavals. Across the world, unprecedented numbers of people employ technology and yet believe in magic. This apparent small-p paradox has shifted the tide of the Ascension War. At the same time that longtime mystics incorporate computer-tech into their lives and rituals, idealistic Technocrats find themselves craving spiritual fulfillment. The so-called Sleepers, meanwhile, have proved themselves to be active agents of both sides, using over-the-counter technology to craft magical visions. From boy wizards to romantic Night-Folk, apocalyptic sagas and CGI superheroism, the pop-culture stew of this millennium fusion represents an embrace of all sides of the Ascension conflict.<br /> <br /> In short, no one side is winning, but all of them \u2013 the Marauders included \u2013 have a chance at capturing a worldwide Consensus.<br /> <br /> The extraordinary citizens of the new millennium are neither the trembling peasants of medieval legend nor the conforming Masses of Technocratic ideals. Instead, they... or, to be more accurate, WE... embrace a vibrant era in which technology, faith, and imagination coexist. The shadow of that era, though, is the potential for global madness and self-inflicted annihilation.<br /> <br /> And that choice, ultimately, lies not with one Awakened faction or the other, but with the extraordinary citizens of the 21st century. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T09:53:14-07:00","id":1522406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win#post1522398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if <b>Mage</b> is a game about collectivism vs. individuality, with the Technocracy representing the former and the Traditions representing the latter</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that &quot;if&quot; needs to advocate for itself a bit more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T10:28:15-07:00","id":1522409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522403#post1522403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that it's a fascinating thing to think about - the tone updates of [x]20 and furor over [x]5 have gotten me thinking about how much of the character of the WoD games is very distinctly a product of the 90s. They're all horror games that reflect the fears of a specific generation. In particular, the generation <i>before</i> mine, so many of the themes don't resonate for me like they did when adolescent-me was looking up to the young-adults of the time. Some of it is almost quaint, now. Don't have time for a full post but I would draw your attention to the &quot;The Rise of the Extraordinary Citizen&quot; sidebar on page 155 of M20:</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to hear more. I'm firmly Gen X, so I get the themes that the game was going for when written. But if it sticks to that, it's going to become obsolete as Gen Xers go away, and will have a dwindling audience until then. So what needs changing to make it resonate more with Millennials? <br /> <br /> As I said in my opening post, the premise of the book is that we're all into a Crisis; so the themes of \u201cthe system is broken\u201d is still <i>very</i> appropriate, at least for now; but that doesn't mean that the whole thing needs to be oriented around the Gen X style nihilism. And in a decade or so, we'll hopefully be past the Crisis; and chances are that if <b>Mage</b> is to remain relevant, it will need to undergo a radical reimagining. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522406#post1522406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that &quot;if&quot; needs to advocate for itself a bit more.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. On that point, I believe that Justin was going to go with that angle for M5 before he left. That said, while the Technocracy is inherently more collectivist than the Traditions are, I don't think that M5 ought to angle for that being the primary conflict, precisely because we're moving into an era where individualism is likely to take a back seat to what Gen X would call collectivism and what Millennials would call community and service; so if you frame M5 in terms of the triumph of the individual, you're forcing the game to lose relevance as that particular theme falls out of favor \u2014 and is likely to remain out of favor for another half-century. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T11:20:39-07:00","id":1522413,"title":"","content":"While my issues with the generational cycle models are many, I'll avoid getting into those because I'm not sure they really matter to what's going to happen to the future of Mage.<br /> <br /> Honestly, however mixed the reception, I think the Disparate Alliance is actually the faction that comes out the best of the current state of affairs because they're the most flexible. If we'll pardon my foray into US politics, the Technocracy and the Traditions are a lot like the current US political parties that count. They've been competing with each other for ages, and in reality make the same decisions on many topics while in power. The small percentages of issues that really disagree with are big issues, but big issues attached to a lot of institutional baggage. Most voters are motivated negatively: they're voting for the least bad choice, not the best of two good choices, or an obvious good choice vs. an obvious bad choice. Even if the US system is in no place for an ascendant third party, the US is also in a place where historically speaking, a new party can displace one of the current top two, or we could see a massive realignment of political alliances that make up each party. The desire for something different, or at least that feels different, is very powerful, and flipping back and forth between two choice stops feeling like &quot;different&quot; pretty quickly.<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance is different. It's not some sort of guarantee that the DA wouldn't just become the Traditions take 2, or even fall into the power-chasing rabbit hole of the Technocracy. But they speak far more to a generation that's tired of both major factions being entrenched in fighting each other, that all the bad actors they could be dealing with are growing in power in the shadow of petty philosophic fights. They can make the case that, &quot;what we have now isn't working, and we have a functional system to try to fix things in a new way,&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T12:17:06-07:00","id":1522418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win#post1522398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title I chose is admittedly click-bait, so don't take it <i>too</i> seriously. But I <i>do</i> want to entertain the possibility that an eventual Technocratic victory in the next decade or so may not only be possible, but maybe even desirable. Bear with me\u2026<br /> <br /> I have been listening to the Audiobook version of <i>The Fourth Turning is Here</i>, which argues that there's a generational cycle of history, with each generation lasting roughly 20 to 25 years or so and having a distinct character that is a reaction to their parents' generation and to which their children will react. This cycle consists of four generations \u2014 currently a Prophet generation (the Boomers), a Nomad generation (Generation X), a Hero generation (the Millennials), and an Artist generation (tentatively called the Homelanders). This cycle drives and is driven by a two-stroke cycle of cycle of spiritual awakenings and civic crises which in their turns remake and reinvigorate the culture (the Awakenings) and the government (the Crises). It's a fascinating read.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, first published in the 90s, is a product of Generation X, and bears our distinctive characteristics: a mixture of pessimism and advocacy for individuality. But according to the theory, we are now firmly in the <i>middle</i> of a Crisis, which shows every indication of being as consequential as the last three Crises: the Great Depression and World War II, the Civil War, and the Revolutionary War. Assuming that this cycle resolved successfully, we'll be living in a distinctly different world in ten years, as different from today as the post-WWII world was from the pre-WWII world, or post-Civil War America was from pre-Civil War America, or the newborn American Republic was from the British colonies that birthed it. And if the past cycles are any indication, the post-Crisis world ten years from now will completely invert the characteristics I described above: expect a more optimistic tone and a tendency to extoll the virtues of community, service, and cooperation over individuality.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to my click-baity title: if <b>Mage</b> is a game about collectivism vs. individuality, with the Technocracy representing the former and the Traditions representing the latter, then chances are that the post-Crisis audience for the game will be firmly on the side of the Technocracy; and if the game doesn't adapt, it may lose whatever relevance it has. So: <i>should</i> <b>Mage</b> (eventually) be remade to that a reformed Technocracy is ascendant, with the Traditions coming to terms with it and possibly even joining forces with it? Or should the game stick to its guns and take the (by then) unpopular position of declaring that the post-Crisis world's likely emphasis on civic-mindedness is fatally flawed, taking <b>MRev</b>'s \u201cThe Ascension War is over, and we lost\u201d attitude up a notch?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy is also representative of imperialism, colonialism, cultural homogeneity, streamlined expression, and various industrial pipelines, so no.<br /> <br /> Collectivism versus individualism is only part of the equation, albeit a very fancy part to look at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T14:06:19-07:00","id":1522423,"title":"","content":"I think that if you go along this line of reasoning and compare it to a nilist society, I imagine that in the M5 the heroes would be the hollow ones and the traditions as well as the technocracy would be controlling doctrines (in fact you could think that the technocracy would be like a tenth tradition in this case). Seriously now, if it were to change then I believe the traditions would use another name, cycles or perhaps covens, and they would be simple ways of using magic or rather telling how to invest it, and some traditions would change a lot, in general they are groups with the same objective, but which don't mix, and the hollow ones would now be a tradition or a separate group, like a wild card.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T02:10:55-07:00","id":1522447,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing: I'm a technocrat at heart, and as flawed as the organization is, I believe they're the best option for the future, but not before some much-needed reforms. Both the traditions and the crafts are a bunch of anachronistic anarchists who cling to belief systems that, quite frankly, offer little to no use for the modern world, but I also defend their right to live as they choose as long as they don't harm anybody.<br /> In any case, I'm one of those fans who believe that the technocracy already &quot;won&quot; but not in the way they wanted or expected. My technocratic agent always smiles with a smirk whenever he sees a traditionalist or a sleeper using a smartphone or any other of the conveniences brought by technology, but here's the thing: he can't control how they use those tools. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar456_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"456\" data-vbnamecard=\"456\">Blackwell</a> said, the sleepers and the mages have taken the dominant paradigm of the technocracy and molded it to their liking. The technocracy may rule, but it doesn't control, which is precisely the only thing it wants. I don't see this as a bad thing, by pushing the paradigm and what can be done with technology the sleepers and the mages are enriching it, bringing some much-needed diversity, flexibility, and creativity to a stagnant vision.<br /> Now, regarding your original question, should the technocracy win? As I said, it already won, so for me the more important questions are these: what technocracy do we want at the helm of humanity's future? Can they create a collectivist vision that brings the most good to the community without harming the rights of the individual? I know it won't happen, but I would love to play a M5 that has these questions at its core, with technocrat agents trying to balance making a world a better place for all without forcing it into homogeneity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 10-09-2023, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T08:01:36-07:00","id":1522458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522447#post1522447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing, I'm a technocrat at heart, and as flawed as the organization is I do believe that they're the best option for the future, but not before some much needed reforms. I also believe that both the traditions and the crafts are a bunch of anacronistic anarchists who cling to belief systems that, quite frankly, offer little to no use for the modern world. Nevertheless I also believe in their right to live as they chose as long as they don't harm anybody.<br /> In any case, I'm one of those fans that believes that the technocracy already &quot;won&quot;, but not in the way they wanted or even expected. My technocratic agent always smiles with a smirk whenever he sees a traditionalist or a sleeper using a smartphone or any other of the conveniencies brought by technology, but here's the thing: he can't control how they use those tools. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar456_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"456\" data-vbnamecard=\"456\">Blackwell</a> said, the sleepers and the mages have taken the dominant paradigm of the technocracy and molded it to their liking. The technocracy may rule, but it doesn't control, which is precisely the only thing it wants. I don't see this as a bad thing, by pushing the paradigm and what can be done with technology the sleepers and the mages are enriching it, bringing some much needed diversity, flexibility, and creativity to a stagnant vision.<br /> Now, regarding your original question, should the technocracy win? As I said, it already won, as such for me the more important questions are this: what technocracy do we want at the helm of humanities future? Can they create a collectivist vision that brings the most good to the community without harming the individual? I know it won't happen, but I would love to play a M5 that has this questions at their core, with technocrat agents trying to balance making a world a better place for all without forcing it into homogeneity.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it were the old WOD it would already be stagnant and rotten like everything else seems to be. A phrase you read in the hermetic tradition book is that by exchanging superstition for science, technocracy created a situation in which both it and traditions lose because the sleepers stop dreaming of trying to innovate, nothing new is created even with technology . Of course, this may be a distorted and totally partial point of view, in this case it IS partial, but partial is not synonymous with wrong. Anyway, one option would be to go that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T09:19:37-07:00","id":1522460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522458#post1522458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it were the old WOD it would already be stagnant and rotten like everything else seems to be. A phrase you read in the hermetic tradition book is that by exchanging superstition for science, technocracy created a situation in which both it and traditions lose because the sleepers stop dreaming of trying to innovate, nothing new is created even with technology . Of course, this may be a distorted and totally partial point of view, in this case, it IS partial, but partial is not synonymous with wrong. Anyway, one option would be to go that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice to know that. The challenge of the technocratic paradigm for me is how to create a safe sandbox for humanity without having that sandbox extinguish their creativity. There can be no growth without freedom and no safety without rules. It's the eternal dilemma of finding the right balance between security and freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T10:17:18-07:00","id":1522464,"title":"","content":"And we keep overcorrecting, which is why the cycle of the generations continues. If post cycles are any indication, the next decade or so will end up with the current Crisis becoming existential; and the forces in the world that <b>Mage</b>'s Technocracy most closely correlates with will end up being instrumental in pulling us through it intact, assuming we <i>do</i> pull through intact. And they'll end up in charge of society as a result, for roughly 40\u201345 years. <br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b>'s 40th Anniversary Edition, if it happens at all, will take place right about the time the current Crisis is resolved. And in <i>that</i> environment, continuing with the notion of the Technocracy as \u201cthe Man\u201d that heroic dissidents struggle against is likely to be a recipe for obsolescence. <br /> <br /> Frankly, it might be better to leave it in obsolescence at that point; Trinity's themes of Hope, Sacrifice, and Unity are more likely to resonate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T15:27:46-07:00","id":1522489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522464#post1522464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we keep overcorrecting, which is why the cycle of the generations continues. If post cycles are any indication, the next decade or so will end up with the current Crisis becoming existential; and the forces in the world that <b>Mage</b>'s Technocracy most closely correlates with will end up being instrumental in pulling us through it intact, assuming we <i>do</i> pull through intact. And they'll end up in charge of society as a result, for roughly 40\u201345 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be committing yourself very firmly to this model.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T20:16:13-07:00","id":1522498,"title":"","content":"So... one of my big problems with this model of generational cycles, is that it is very focused on Western industrial societies. It really breaks down if you go earlier than the Industrial revolution in Europe, and doesn't apply to all sorts of cases where the &quot;crisis&quot; was European colonialism and imperialism that didn't get &quot;solved&quot; in a generational time-frame. It also ignores how subcultures (esp. minorities) do not experience these cycles in the same way.<br /> <br /> As an example of all of that: Haiti and the Indemnity issue. When Haiti revolted against France, and won the ground war for independence, the French demanded payments (indemnity) before they would recognize the Haitian government, for their loses during the revolt... including the value of the slaves that had been emancipated. While France eventually sold the debt, it never forgave the debt, and to this day refuses any claim that they hold responsibility for the impact of that debt and should have to give that money back. It took 122 years for Haiti to finally pay off that debt, and that crushing financial burden improvised the nation far more than other countries that won independence in the same period without that hanging over their heads. Haiti is still struggling to overcome the setbacks of over a century of inability to grow economically. That &quot;crisis&quot; lasting 122 years, and impacting well beyond that, means that industrial generational cycle never really set in. It has just been ongoing crisis.<br /> <br /> The problem with how to keep Mage relevant and using this particular model, is that an Industrial era model is unlikely to be relevant if we actually manage to solve many of our current macro-social problems. Trying to predict based on a model that most likely isn't going to survive future changes isn't really functional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T20:53:41-07:00","id":1522499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522464#post1522464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we keep overcorrecting, which is why the cycle of the generations continues. If post cycles are any indication, the next decade or so will end up with the current Crisis becoming existential; and the forces in the world that <b>Mage</b>'s Technocracy most closely correlates with will end up being instrumental in pulling us through it intact, assuming we <i>do</i> pull through intact. And they'll end up in charge of society as a result, for roughly 40\u201345 years.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b>'s 40th Anniversary Edition, if it happens at all, will take place right about the time the current Crisis is resolved. And in <i>that</i> environment, continuing with the notion of the Technocracy as \u201cthe Man\u201d that heroic dissidents struggle against is likely to be a recipe for obsolescence.<br /> <br /> Frankly, it might be better to leave it in obsolescence at that point; Trinity's themes of Hope, Sacrifice, and Unity are more likely to resonate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to say what the future of Mage is at this point. Though if it keeps with the general idea of what's in M20, the Technocracy will continue to the group that while having fallen from the noble ideals of their forebears, are striving to make the world better. Hell since the missing four Rev Ed CBs were released, we've seen the Technocracy moving further away from their original Western White Man outlook to a more diverse and global Technocratic Union with <i>Technocracy Reloaded </i>regarding the Technocracy of the 90s as rather antiquated relic that looks silly and dated today. It even straight up has the Union utterly frustrated by how the United States has turned out in recent years with some wanting to just label it a failed experiment and move on. Something that even the Rev Ed at it's most nihilistic would have taught was absurd.<br /> <br /> For that matter, even for as much as Victorian Mage slams the Order of Reason and labels them the villains, it still points out all the good the OoR is doing alongside the bad and that every Convention has good aspects to them, not just the future VE, SoE and VA.<br /> <br /> If Mage continues with where we're at right now, the likely state will be a situation not unlike what it was during MtSC, with the Traditions and Technocracy (and Disparate Alliance if they're kept around) in a murkier, less antagonistic state between each other. Some times they will fight each other, some times they will work together to deal with a problem and other times they will just keep a weary distance from each other. Meanwhile the Nephandi become a much more serious threat (which let's face it with what they are, they really should have been from the start), taking that mantle of the major antagonist faction. The Technocracy will, like I said above, continuing it's trend of reforming and struggling against problems internal and external as it becomes a more global Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Of course again, that assumes the general trajectory of Mage continues from where M20's at which we can't really say at this moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T03:35:02-07:00","id":1522505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522498#post1522498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... one of my big problems with this model of generational cycles, is that it is very focused on Western industrial societies.</div> </div> </div> </div> More specifically, it's focused on England and the United States, going back to the Elizabethan era: the first Crisis of the civilization in question came to a head with the English defeat of the Spanish Armada. The book talks about how other societies have the notion of cyclic time but don't experience generational cycles, but that the Western notion of linear time (modernity) has paradoxically given rise to cycles that don't exist in cultures that don't similarly push the idea of time as a progression. That it \u201cbreaks down\u201d elsewhere isn't a flaw; it's not attempting to be universal. But it <i>does</i> apply to the United States; and it is in full effect today. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522498#post1522498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with how to keep Mage relevant and using this particular model, is that an Industrial era model is unlikely to be relevant if we actually manage to solve many of our current macro-social problems. Trying to predict based on a model that most likely isn't going to survive future changes isn't really functional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that, as things stand, it's too late to avoid the Crisis: not only are all of the elements already in place for it, but we're already over halfway through it; we just haven't seen the final transformative stages yet. It <i>is</i> possible to influence the details of how it will resolve, though that partly depends on exactly what will trigger its final stage; and it's unlikely that we'll know what that will be until just before it happens.<br /> <br /> And not only are we going to go through the remainder of the Crisis, but the subsequent High is just as inevitable, as everything needed to push it through is <i>also</i> already in place. The earliest opportunity we have to get out of the cycle is after that, by convincing the kids of the Millennials not to raise their kids the way the Boomers were raised. Which is what they're likely to do without a concerted effort to convince them otherwise. <br /> <br /> But that goes well beyond the subject of this thread: if the cycle continues, the earliest that Mage's original themes will be relevant again will be in about sixty years, when the next Awakening begins. And if I'm still alive for that (I'm 51, and will be over 100 by then), I'll be impressed that Mage has survived for so long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T05:31:42-07:00","id":1522509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522499#post1522499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hard to say what the future of Mage is at this point. Though if it keeps with the general idea of what's in M20, the Technocracy will continue to the group that while having fallen from the noble ideals of their forebears, are striving to make the world better. Hell since the missing four Rev Ed CBs were released, we've seen the Technocracy moving further away from their original Western White Man outlook to a more diverse and global Technocratic Union with <i>Technocracy Reloaded </i>regarding the Technocracy of the 90s as rather antiquated relic that looks silly and dated today. It even straight up has the Union utterly frustrated by how the United States has turned out in recent years with some wanting to just label it a failed experiment and move on. Something that even the Rev Ed at it's most nihilistic would have taught was absurd.<br /> <br /> For that matter, even for as much as Victorian Mage slams the Order of Reason and labels them the villains, it still points out all the good the OoR is doing alongside the bad and that every Convention has good aspects to them, not just the future VE, SoE and VA.<br /> <br /> If Mage continues with where we're at right now, the likely state will be a situation not unlike what it was during MtSC, with the Traditions and Technocracy (and Disparate Alliance if they're kept around) in a murkier, less antagonistic state between each other. Some times they will fight each other, some times they will work together to deal with a problem and other times they will just keep a weary distance from each other. Meanwhile the Nephandi become a much more serious threat (which let's face it with what they are, they really should have been from the start), taking that mantle of the major antagonist faction. The Technocracy will, like I said above, continuing it's trend of reforming and struggling against problems internal and external as it becomes a more global Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Of course again, that assumes the general trajectory of Mage continues from where M20's at which we can't really say at this moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>My premise here is that the Real World\u2122 trajectory isn't going to be what it is in ten years; that we're primed for a drastic change comparable to the Revolutionary War, the Civil War, or World War II, and at this point are just waiting for the spark that will trigger it. And Mage will surely change in accord to that. <br /> <br /> And while there's no way to predict what will trigger it or what the exact nature of that change will be, we <i>can</i> be confident that it will result in a resurgence in appreciation for the positive aspects of what the Technocracy represents. And in <i>that</i> environment, I wonder if a hypothetical M40 might be better off portraying something closer to an <i>alliance</i> between the Traditions and a reformed Technocracy for a better future, with the old model of \u201cthe world is going to Hell in a handbasket\u201d being relegated to the dustbin of history once the Crisis is over and the subsequent High begins. <br /> <br /> As I see it, there will still be room for the Traditions in this new model, and they'll still be in opposition to the Technocracy; but it will be less a matter of an Ascension War and more a matter of trying to promote individuality and a healthy sense of rebellion in a world that no longer has any interest in such things. This also has historical precedent: most recently, the post-WWII era had writers who were lamenting the shallowness and conformity of the age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T12:13:56-07:00","id":1522527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522505#post1522505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> More specifically, it's focused on England and the United States, going back to the Elizabethan era: the first Crisis of the civilization in question came to a head with the English defeat of the Spanish Armada. The book talks about how other societies have the notion of cyclic time but don't experience generational cycles, but that the Western notion of linear time (modernity) has paradoxically given rise to cycles that don't exist in cultures that don't similarly push the idea of time as a progression. That it \u201cbreaks down\u201d elsewhere isn't a flaw; it's not attempting to be universal. But it <i>does</i> apply to the United States; and it is in full effect today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd hope that 26 years later Howe would have refined his theories a little, but it sounds like it's still as cherry-picked and bias-selected as it was the first time he tried to make this case (it feels a bit on the nose that he's trying again 26 years later to try to do what many prognosticators do and retrofit new data that doesn't their model into somehow supporting it though obvious vagueness in the initial predictions).<br /> <br /> Though my mind boggles that anyone things that the big &quot;Crisis&quot; for England was... the Spanish Armada (which, there were a bunch of them during the Spanish-Engish proxy conflicts/unofficial war?)... when the death of Elizabeth the I and her having no publicly declared successor was a massive &quot;Crisis&quot; and the following century of Stuart rule of England didn't follow Howe's model at all (since it was a century of near continuous unresolved tension between Protestants and Catholics in England that the Stuarts never managed to sort out on that generational cycle, and the ascension of the Hanovers was far more what shaped English (and American) cultural history going forward.<br /> <br /> And of course Howe's disregard for minority experiences seems to have continued, which might have been excusable in the 90s, but the US's growing ethnic diversity means you can't just look at white middle/upper class social trends and really have much to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that, as things stand, it's too late to avoid the Crisis: </div> </div> </div>I didn't say we could? It's clear that the US is at an inflection point in history, but that doesn't prove this particular model of generation cycles is valid at all, let alone predictive of what will happen in the next two decades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And not only are we going to go through the remainder of the Crisis, but the subsequent High is just as inevitable,... </div> </div> </div>See, that's the problem. No, it isn't. There is no historical precedent for a civilization that lasts forever. It's never happened that no matter how many crises and rebirths a civilization goes through, it is manifestly inevitable that all future inflection points will turn into new high points. Optimism is fine and dandy, but it isn't destiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T20:32:54-07:00","id":1522553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522509#post1522509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My premise here is that the Real World\u2122 trajectory isn't going to be what it is in ten years; that we're primed for a drastic change comparable to the Revolutionary War, the Civil War, or World War II, and at this point are just waiting for the spark that will trigger it. And Mage will surely change in accord to that.<br /> <br /> And while there's no way to predict what will trigger it or what the exact nature of that change will be, we <i>can</i> be confident that it will result in a resurgence in appreciation for the positive aspects of what the Technocracy represents. And in <i>that</i> environment, I wonder if a hypothetical M40 might be better off portraying something closer to an <i>alliance</i> between the Traditions and a reformed Technocracy for a better future, with the old model of \u201cthe world is going to Hell in a handbasket\u201d being relegated to the dustbin of history once the Crisis is over and the subsequent High begins.<br /> <br /> As I see it, there will still be room for the Traditions in this new model, and they'll still be in opposition to the Technocracy; but it will be less a matter of an Ascension War and more a matter of trying to promote individuality and a healthy sense of rebellion in a world that no longer has any interest in such things. This also has historical precedent: most recently, the post-WWII era had writers who were lamenting the shallowness and conformity of the age.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's highly unlikely we'd ever see a lasting Tradition/Technocracy alliance or ceasefire. While they may agree with some things, there's plenty of others that simply don't. Then there's the matter of their clashing beliefs. Like we know that some Tradition Mages that are actively supporting alternative medicine not just because it undermines the Technocratic Paradigm but supports their own Paradigms.<br /> <br /> The Ascension War isn't just going to go away after such an alliance because the Ascension War has <i>always</i> been happening. Yes, when most people talk about it they are specifically talking about the conflict between the Traditions and Technocracy but the true Ascension War long predates those groups. It's been raging since the earliest Mages began to develop their Paradigms and strove to present that Paradigm as the Truth of the Universe. And when you believe at the very core of your being that you have the Truth of the Universe only to encounter others with their own Truths different from yours that they believe just as hard as you, there's going to be conflict. After all, that's part of the reason the Traditions spent centuries loosing ground to the Order of Reason, their differing Beliefs and previous conflicts with each other prevented them from truly uniting. Even the modern Conventions despite sharing a Paradigm have differences of belief and internal tensions caused by those differences.<br /> <br /> Even if they band together to solve some global crisis, they're going to butt heads over <i>how</i> to solve the problem. Hell, both groups are likely to have their own infighting on how to solve the problems as well.<br /> <br /> Any Tradition/Technocracy alliance cannot last because at the end of the day, MtAs is all the Conflict of Beliefs and they have very different Beliefs. The best we could get is a deescalation of tensions. They'll never be fully gone but they won't be as great as they were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T22:13:16-07:00","id":1522558,"title":"","content":"Somehow I guess this discussion started to diverge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T07:23:32-07:00","id":1522793,"title":"","content":"Well - beyond the fact that I don't fell inclied to believe in that predictive model -,my answer in a more general sense would be *no*. No, because then we wouldn't have antagonists.<br /> <br /> To elaborate: The conflict between the Traditoions and the Technocracy was always at the core of Mage.<br /> *This is <i>especially</i> the case if the Technocracy are the good guys protagonist, because &quot;good guys&quot; need something evil to figth against.<br /> *This is <i>also especially the case</i> if they're not good but &quot;gray&quot; and &quot;flawed&quot;, because gray and flawed protagonists require antagonists to give <i>weigth </i>to their moral dilemas<br /> *I see a Technocratic win if they're the antagonists of an underdog. Like, say, roughly what's described on Mage 1e.<br /> <br /> <i>Protagonists</i>, in general, need something to &quot;agonize&quot; against - this is a narrative need that's older than human history. And while antagonism doesn't need to take the form of something tangible, it's still very important. Maybe more so than who's the protag.<br /> <br /> Like, on it's face the idea of figthing &quot;shallowness and conformity&quot; isn't a bad one. but w/o a conflict between/against Technocrats and/or Traditionalists I don't see where or how that conflict would manifest on Mage.<br /> <br /> Like, do they <i>manifest </i>as a phisical danger to our reality like <i>Nobilis excrucians</i>?<br /> Is Paradox now more antagonistic than ever?, manifesting forces of conformity bent on breaking magick and science alike, <s>doing terrible 5 editions, :P , sorry, I couldn't resist</s>, and has to be stop?<br /> <br /> Not all antagonistic forces need to be <i>present </i>nor <i>a faction on a shadowy war</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, but Mage it's built in a way to facilitate those stories. Like, you could have <i>nature </i>as an antagonist on a <i>survival</i> game - but Mage systems don't precisely facilitate that, and I would probably <i>not</i> <i>play Mage</i> if I wanted to play such a game. So, these things need to be well established\u200b <hr /><br /> Working with what we have: I think that, on Mage, the Technocracy and the Traditions are currently the richest, most well developped, factions to form protagonists and antagonists (in a Narrative sense, I.E, they have complex motives to reach their goals, that could be dystopic very easily depending on how you look at them, they have the means to reach them).<br /> <br /> Nephandi and Marauders are too simple to provide a consistent role as either.<br /> <br /> Talking to the modern issues, I have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> , the Disparate alliance seems to be the choice for a protagonist. Perhaps against antagonistic, and ascendant, Traditions/Technocrats.<br /> Altrough I'm very critical to the Disparate as they're represented in M20, and I think a lot of changes are due, the &quot;core&quot; idea of<i> accepting diversity as diverse,</i> instead of trying to syncretize everything <i>seems </i>like something one can spin on current trends, and on the Alliance<br /> <br /> Anything more than that, I think, would require not the Technocracy as winners, but rather a very different game, with different rules, lore and protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-19-2023, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T13:03:59-07:00","id":1522798,"title":"","content":"The general concept of Mage was that the game (and the entire World of Darkness line) was set in a world where magic was dying and the supernatural was becoming more and more scarce. However, there was going to come a point where the End of the World happens, and just before that began, magic would likely flood back into our world, as that is what would be necessary for the powers of Evil to take control of the world before the Final Battle would begin. There are many other books and media that follow this general path, so it is by no means unique to WoD.<br /> <br /> I don't see why that would need to change at all. It is a good set up and allows a lot of leeway for STs and excitement for PCs. Using that general concept, you can set WoD/Mage games in any era of history, in any culture, and you'll still have a fun game that satisfies any requirements for a WoD/Mage game.<br /> <br /> The Fourth Turning is an interesting book, but like all &quot;history is in cycles!&quot; books, it is pseudoscience. Its merits as predictive future is extremely dubious, and I don't see its relevance to this game.<br /> <br /> Likely, the Technocracy will be shown as increasing its power and the Traditions see further erosion as we head into a future that is becoming more dominated by science. But to what extent that substantially changes the premise of the original corebooks is probably marginal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T06:24:43-07:00","id":1523816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522403#post1522403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that it's a fascinating thing to think about - the tone updates of [x]20 and furor over [x]5 have gotten me thinking about how much of the character of the WoD games is very distinctly a product of the 90s. They're all horror games that reflect the fears of a specific generation. In particular, the generation <i>before</i> mine, so many of the themes don't resonate for me like they did when adolescent-me was looking up to the young-adults of the time. Some of it is almost quaint, now. Don't have time for a full post but I would draw your attention to the &quot;The Rise of the Extraordinary Citizen&quot; sidebar on page 155 of M20:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fellow millennial like me huh?<br /> <br /> The other generations don't seem to like us very much... Something about us being &quot;spoiled&quot; or something....<br /> <br /> Still, if this &quot;Forth Turning&quot; idea is correct (and it does seem like we are living a period of Crisis), we are supposed to be the generation of &quot;heroes&quot;, so be prepared...<br /> <br /> And yes, WoD is absolutely a Gen X thing, which is why for Millennials like us it all just sounds so cartoonishly off.<br /> <br /> It's fun, undoubtedly, but just so absolutely off the mark for us.<br /> <br /> I wonder how the antisocial Gen Z views it (just don't tell them that it is a product of their parents generation, this will be our little secret)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T06:42:45-07:00","id":1523817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522409#post1522409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to hear more. I'm firmly Gen X, so I get the themes that the game was going for when written. But if it sticks to that, it's going to become obsolete as Gen Xers go away, and will have a dwindling audience until then. So what needs changing to make it resonate more with Millennials?<br /> <br /> As I said in my opening post, the premise of the book is that we're all into a Crisis; so the themes of \u201cthe system is broken\u201d is still <i>very</i> appropriate, at least for now; but that doesn't mean that the whole thing needs to be oriented around the Gen X style nihilism. And in a decade or so, we'll hopefully be past the Crisis; and chances are that if <b>Mage</b> is to remain relevant, it will need to undergo a radical reimagining.<br /> <br /> Agreed. On that point, I believe that Justin was going to go with that angle for M5 before he left. That said, while the Technocracy is inherently more collectivist than the Traditions are, I don't think that M5 ought to angle for that being the primary conflict, precisely because we're moving into an era where individualism is likely to take a back seat to what Gen X would call collectivism and what Millennials would call community and service; so if you frame M5 in terms of the triumph of the individual, you're forcing the game to lose relevance as that particular theme falls out of favor \u2014 and is likely to remain out of favor for another half-century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah, millennials are boring! Look at the literature that my generation have as our bullmark... Harry Potter!<br /> <br /> You have a wand, you fly in a stick and at the end of the day, you win not because you're competent or because you're smart, but because you are SPECIAL!<br /> <br /> \ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd22<br /> <br /> Yeah, I agree with the Gen X criticism: we millennials are SPOILED. A trait we inherited by our Boomer parents (psss, but don't tell any millennials this, we will never admit it - this can be our little secret).<br /> <br /> Millennials are teamworkers however, unlike the Gen Z who are antisocial (that's the fault of YOUR Gen X), so I'm more worried about Gen Z take than on the game than ours.<br /> <br /> Just to illustrate, I, as a typical Millennial (and as spoiled as any other), after the mythical WoD &quot;end of the world&quot; (now that's some Gen X if I have ever seen one) once concocted a small &quot;continuation&quot; in my head... The dispersed Techies on Earth, shattered as they were, begin to make arrangements with the also shattered Traditions (it was the time of the 3rd edition and Avatar Storm and all that).<br /> <br /> In the end, they &quot;save the world&quot; together and the Technocracy still rules, but now they make accomodations for more &quot;diversity&quot; - allow for a bit more of &quot;religious freedom&quot; if you will, in a very resumed way, and they all lived happily ever after.<br /> <br /> Blergh \ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd22. So boring. Typical Millennial fantasy, I'll admit. But there's something interesting in this: at the time I created that story, I wasn't familiar with the idea of the &quot;Forth Turning&quot; yet, however in my fantasy I subconsciously followed all that is described under it: society going under a Crisis, and the &quot;Hero Generation&quot; coalescing under a single goal towards achieving unity.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I think this helps to illustrate a bit about how the mind of a Millennial works. We all have dreams about unity and &quot;overcoming differences towards achieving a greater goal&quot;. Blergh, all that sunshine and unicorns is disgusting I know, but that's how we Millennials are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T06:51:00-07:00","id":1523818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522447#post1522447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing, I'm a technocrat at heart, and as flawed as the organization is I do believe that they're the best option for the future, but not before some much needed reforms. I also believe that both the traditions and the crafts are a bunch of anacronistic anarchists who cling to belief systems that, quite frankly, offer little to no use for the modern world. Nevertheless I also believe in their right to live as they chose as long as they don't harm anybody.<br /> In any case, I'm one of those fans that believes that the technocracy already &quot;won&quot;, but not in the way they wanted or even expected. My technocratic agent always smiles with a smirk whenever he sees a traditionalist or a sleeper using a smartphone or any other of the conveniencies brought by technology, but here's the thing: he can't control how they use those tools. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar456_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"456\" data-vbnamecard=\"456\">Blackwell</a> said, the sleepers and the mages have taken the dominant paradigm of the technocracy and molded it to their liking. The technocracy may rule, but it doesn't control, which is precisely the only thing it wants. I don't see this as a bad thing, by pushing the paradigm and what can be done with technology the sleepers and the mages are enriching it, bringing some much needed diversity, flexibility, and creativity to a stagnant vision.<br /> Now, regarding your original question, should the technocracy win? As I said, it already won, as such for me the more important questions are this: what technocracy do we want at the helm of humanities future? Can they create a collectivist vision that brings the most good to the community without harming the individual? I know it won't happen, but I would love to play a M5 that has this questions at their core, with technocrat agents trying to balance making a world a better place for all without forcing it into homogeneity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That's the Millennial thought process right over there. If you read my previous post, that's EXACTLY what my &quot;fantasy prediction&quot; held. The Techies reforming and allowing the Trads to &quot;live and let live&quot; in a Hare Krishna world of happy people holding hands (\ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd22).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T07:06:29-07:00","id":1523820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522553#post1522553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's highly unlikely we'd ever see a lasting Tradition/Technocracy alliance or ceasefire. While they may agree with some things, there's plenty of others that simply don't. Then there's the matter of their clashing beliefs. Like we know that some Tradition Mages that are actively supporting alternative medicine not just because it undermines the Technocratic Paradigm but supports their own Paradigms.<br /> <br /> The Ascension War isn't just going to go away after such an alliance because the Ascension War has <i>always</i> been happening. Yes, when most people talk about it they are specifically talking about the conflict between the Traditions and Technocracy but the true Ascension War long predates those groups. It's been raging since the earliest Mages began to develop their Paradigms and strove to present that Paradigm as the Truth of the Universe. And when you believe at the very core of your being that you have the Truth of the Universe only to encounter others with their own Truths different from yours that they believe just as hard as you, there's going to be conflict. After all, that's part of the reason the Traditions spent centuries loosing ground to the Order of Reason, their differing Beliefs and previous conflicts with each other prevented them from truly uniting. Even the modern Conventions despite sharing a Paradigm have differences of belief and internal tensions caused by those differences.<br /> <br /> Even if they band together to solve some global crisis, they're going to butt heads over <i>how</i> to solve the problem. Hell, both groups are likely to have their own infighting on how to solve the problems as well.<br /> <br /> Any Tradition/Technocracy alliance cannot last because at the end of the day, MtAs is all the Conflict of Beliefs and they have very different Beliefs. The best we could get is a deescalation of tensions. They'll never be fully gone but they won't be as great as they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagined a world where, instead of open war, their conflict becomes a lot more of an &quot;academic&quot; issue. The Techies and Trads ally with each other, and reach a &quot;consensus&quot; (not to mistake it with &quot;Consensus&quot;) to let the masses decide by themselves, instead of forcing their views unto them.<br /> <br /> This also better reflects the real world by the way... The world is filled with esoteric, pseudoscientific or conspiratorial lunacy, instead of just cold and rational Science. Thus, the Techies firmly believe they can keep things under control, since at the end of the day they are sure the masses will choose &quot;da Science&quot;, the Traditions are happy because now they at least have a chance to introduce their esoterica into the masses, even if not able to impose their own views, and both are happy because they now have more time and resources to dedicate towards hunting down pan dimensional demons and things-men-were-not-meant-to-know.<br /> <br /> There would still be a lot of political backstabbing, sometimes literal backstabbings (and all the consequences of those), some rogues in both sides causing trouble and whatnot, but not all out full scale war. A different scenario from what is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T07:14:08-07:00","id":1523821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1523817#post1523817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bah, millennials are boring! Look at the literature that my generation have as our bullmark... Harry Potter!<br /> <br /> You have a wand, you fly in a stick and at the end of the day, you win not because you're competent or because you're smart, but because you are SPECIAL!<br /> <br /> \ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd22<br /> <br /> Yeah, I agree with the Gen X criticism: we millennials are SPOILED. A trait we inherited by our Boomer parents (psss, but don't tell any millennials this, we will never admit it - this can be our little secret).<br /> <br /> Millennials are teamworkers however, unlike the Gen Z who are antisocial (that's the fault of YOUR Gen X), so I'm more worried about Gen Z take than on the game than ours.<br /> <br /> Just to illustrate, I, as a typical Millennial (and as spoiled as any other), after the mythical WoD &quot;end of the world&quot; (now that's some Gen X if I have ever seen one) once concocted a small &quot;continuation&quot; in my head... The dispersed Techies on Earth, shattered as they were, begin to make arrangements with the also shattered Traditions (it was the time of the 3rd edition and Avatar Storm and all that).<br /> <br /> In the end, they &quot;save the world&quot; together and the Technocracy still rules, but now they make accomodations for more &quot;diversity&quot; - allow for a bit more of &quot;religious freedom&quot; if you will, in a very resumed way, and they all lived happily ever after.<br /> <br /> Blergh \ud83e\udd22\ud83e\udd22. So boring. Typical Millennial fantasy, I'll admit. But there's something interesting in this: at the time I created that story, I wasn't familiar with the idea of the &quot;Forth Turning&quot; yet, however in my fantasy I subconsciously followed all that is described under it: society going under a Crisis, and the &quot;Hero Generation&quot; coalescing under a single goal towards achieving unity.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I think this helps to illustrate a bit about how the mind of a Millennial works. We all have dreams about unity and &quot;overcoming differences towards achieving a greater goal&quot;. Blergh, all that sunshine and unicorns is disgusting I know, but that's how we Millennials are.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis illustrates why I \u201cput stock\u201d in the Strauss-Howe generational theory: it's <i>not </i>positing some abstract, universal cycle driven by abstract, impersonal forces; it's rooted in very believable psychological dynamics of children be shaped by their upbringing and their tendency to overcompensate for their parents' perceived failings. And the fact that it <i>isn't </i>running like clockwork is, ironically, a mark in its favor as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> And yet, every generation seems to think that <i>their </i>fix will persist \u2014 that the future that they create will continue on the same trajectory without alteration by future generations. And/or they worry that their kids will \u201cscrew it up\u201d \u2014 which they likely will. And the reason I feel like the near future is the generational cycle is inevitable is because the Millennials are already here and \u201cGen Z\u201d/the \u201cHomelanders\u201d/whatever they end up being called (it's too soon to name them) are already being raised. The \u201cdamage\u201d, as it were, has already been done. Maybe if you guys don't make the same child-rearing mistakes that the GI generation did, we won't get another Boomer-like generation after \u201cGen Z\u201d \u2014 though I'm on the fence as to whether that would be a good thing or a bad thing. Regardless, it's further down the road than I'm prepared to look right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Adding context 10-08-2023, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T07:27:39-07:00","id":1523822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1523820#post1523820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagined a world where, instead of open war, their conflict becomes a lot more of an &quot;academic&quot; issue. The Techies and Trads ally with each other, and reach a &quot;consensus&quot; (not to mistake it with &quot;Consensus&quot;) to let the masses decide by themselves, instead of forcing their views unto them.<br /> <br /> This also better reflects the real world by the way... The world is filled with esoteric, pseudoscientific or conspiratorial lunacy, instead of just cold and rational Science. Thus, the Techies firmly believe they can keep things under control, since at the end of the day they are sure the masses will choose &quot;da Science&quot;, the Traditions are happy because now they at least have a chance to introduce their esoterica into the masses, even if not able to impose their own views, and both are happy because they now have more time and resources to dedicate towards hunting down pan dimensional demons and things-men-were-not-meant-to-know.<br /> <br /> There would still be a lot of political backstabbing, sometimes literal backstabbings (and all the consequences of those), some rogues in both sides causing trouble and whatnot, but not all out full scale war. A different scenario from what is now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. And according to the aforementioned generational theory, the High that follows a Crisis isn't a time of peace, per se, except in comparison; there's still conflict and wars. But it's not the full scale all out war that a Crisis ends up as (e.g., the Revolutionary War, the Civil War, and World War II); there's a difference in character of wars and conflicts during a High, where they tend to be more about resolving lingering disagreements than with fighting to bring down/restructure the entire order of things. Once we get through the current Crisis (successfully or not; I'm not saying this as a mark of optimism), we're not likely to see the conditions suitable to another one arise until the early 22nd century, at a point where even today's Millennials will likely be gone (barring medical advances and extended lifespans).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T19:31:13-07:00","id":1524081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1523822#post1523822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. And according to the aforementioned generational theory, the High that follows a Crisis isn't a time of peace, per se, except in comparison; there's still conflict and wars. But it's not the full scale all out war that a Crisis ends up as (e.g., the Revolutionary War, the Civil War, and World War II); there's a difference in character of wars and conflicts during a High, where they tend to be more about resolving lingering disagreements than with fighting to bring down/restructure the entire order of things. Once we get through the current Crisis (successfully or not; I'm not saying this as a mark of optimism), we're not likely to see the conditions suitable to another one arise until the early 22nd century, at a point where even today's Millennials will likely be gone (barring medical advances and extended lifespans).</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't count on us millennials being gone by the 22nd century mate! I'll be a steroid filled cyborg at my prime, lecturing the younglings about the depravity of their ways and about how &quot;in the good ol' days, that's how we've done it kids!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T05:49:03-08:00","id":1527547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1522409#post1522409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to hear more. I'm firmly Gen X, so I get the themes that the game was going for when written. But if it sticks to that, it's going to become obsolete as Gen Xers go away, and will have a dwindling audience until then. So what needs changing to make it resonate more with Millennials?<br /> <br /> As I said in my opening post, the premise of the book is that we're all into a Crisis; so the themes of \u201cthe system is broken\u201d is still <i>very</i> appropriate, at least for now; but that doesn't mean that the whole thing needs to be oriented around the Gen X style nihilism. And in a decade or so, we'll hopefully be past the Crisis; and chances are that if <b>Mage</b> is to remain relevant, it will need to undergo a radical reimagining.<br /> <br /> Agreed. On that point, I believe that Justin was going to go with that angle for M5 before he left. That said, while the Technocracy is inherently more collectivist than the Traditions are, I don't think that M5 ought to angle for that being the primary conflict, precisely because we're moving into an era where individualism is likely to take a back seat to what Gen X would call collectivism and what Millennials would call community and service; so if you frame M5 in terms of the triumph of the individual, you're forcing the game to lose relevance as that particular theme falls out of favor \u2014 and is likely to remain out of favor for another half-century.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a millennial and I think the Technocracy are monsterous fascists, and I'm pretty far left by American standards. Just because a faction or society is collectivist doesn't mean they're good. It's what they do that matters.<br /> <br /> Maosit China, Nordic wellfare states and Nazi Germany are all collectivist. Only one them in my opinion is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T18:48:23-08:00","id":1527587,"title":"","content":"Should the Technocracy win?<br /> <br /> No. Next!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T05:25:23-08:00","id":1527832,"title":"","content":"*shrug* I think it would be fine if the Technos won. Honestly, Traditions vs Technos is kind of low-stakes. They both want humanity to become more prosperous. Does it really matter whether that's because the world looks like Star Trek, or a Hermetic fantasy land where any mundane person can create Star Trek-like effects by drawing hermetic symbols and saying certain latin phrases in highly specific orders? It's the Nephandi who are dangerous. Everyone else is arguing about whether it is better to cure cancer with a pill, or by praying to The One. As long as humanity gains some consensus method of curing cancer, who cares which group achieves it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T10:18:15-08:00","id":1527853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1527832#post1527832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug* I think it would be fine if the Technos won. Honestly, Traditions vs Technos is kind of low-stakes. They both want humanity to become more prosperous. Does it really matter whether that's because the world looks like Star Trek, or a Hermetic fantasy land where any mundane person can create Star Trek-like effects by drawing hermetic symbols and saying certain latin phrases in highly specific orders? It's the Nephandi who are dangerous. Everyone else is arguing about whether it is better to cure cancer with a pill, or by praying to The One. As long as humanity gains some consensus method of curing cancer, who cares which group achieves it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! Sanity! You better be careful on these boards very few of these folks tolerate common sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T10:29:34-08:00","id":1527854,"title":"","content":"I would like to see the Traditions win, but I also wouldn\u2019t mind a future in which the Technocracy and the Traditions work together for the greater good of humanity. In terms of generations, I was born into Gen X, but I definitely don\u2019t think like them. I\u2019m much more like a Millennial or even Gen Z (the term Artist Generation for Gen Z really resonates with me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T10:49:08-08:00","id":1527857,"title":"","content":"If you separate the Technocracy from its methods and its social values and only look at the good things they want to do for humanity, they're going to look very good. Same for the Traditions. It's not really about how either side cures cancer, its about what they do to humanity and reality while they are curing cancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T11:08:47-08:00","id":1527859,"title":"","content":"Frankly, most of the Trad mages are long over any anti technology bias. A Star Trek/Jetsons future, as long as Magic and Spirituality are recognized parts of it, would be okay with most Trad Mages. <br /> <br /> The main problem really comes from the NWO and the Syndicate. Sure, the Progenitors freak out over magical healing, but that could be managed. Both the NWO and the Syndicate are desperate to control, limit, and define others. The Ali Batini have a similar problem, as do the Templers. If the NWO rules the world, reality would look like the Village on <b>The Prisoner.</b> The Syndicate ruling reality would lead to the kinds of social inequality typical of Cyberpunk dystopias. The Ali Batini and the Templars, and the Sisters of Hypolyta, would create low tech dystopias of rigid control and conformity. The Hollow Ones, for all their eternal rebellion, would be little different. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T11:33:50-08:00","id":1527862,"title":"","content":"\u2026which is why the original post posited at least some degree of reform in the Union. Obviously, if the most dystopian version of the Technocracy wins, it would be a disaster.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Note also that I gave reasons for the reform: Mage was first published in the early 90s, at a time when the general zeitgeist featured a thoroughly corrupt and irredeemable Man oppressing everyone. We're now 30 years later, and the zeitgeist has changed: now, it's even more apparent than ever that the system is broken; but there's also a growing attitude among the younger generation that it can't and should be fixed. And there's reason to think that one way or the other, the current crisis <i>will </i>be resolved, and sober rather than later. The world will not be as it is in ten years, any more than it is now what it was ten years ago. <br /> <br /> So going on the premise that the system will undergo some sort of reform in the near future that will lead to a world where trust in the system gets restored, and noting that the Technocracy in many ways serves as the in-game stand-in for \u201cthe system\u201d, that implies some sort of reform to the Technocracy that fixes its most broken aspects. With <i>that </i>happening, should the Technocracy win? Not \u201cthe Technocracy at its worst\u201d or even \u201cthe Technocracy as it is now\u201d, but rather the Technocracy that I'm anticipating. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-03-2024, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T16:37:15-08:00","id":1527963,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think the Hollow Ones are that bad\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T18:12:07-08:00","id":1527966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1527963#post1527963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think the Hollow Ones are that bad\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Many Hollow Ones are noble, large numbers of Hollow Ones are <i>Obsessive </i>Romantic Revolutionaries. They're up on Rosinante and tilting with windmills at the snap of fingers. Most of the Sane/Honorable ones joined the Trads after the fall of Horizon. <br /> <br /> Now, maybe in your game the Hollow Ones didn't betray the Traditions. In that case they might be a better group of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T21:15:31-08:00","id":1527975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1527966#post1527966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many Hollow Ones are noble, large numbers of Hollow Ones are <i>Obsessive </i>Romantic Revolutionaries. They're up on Rosinante and tilting with windmills at the snap of fingers. Most of the Sane/Honorable ones joined the Trads after the fall of Horizon.<br /> <br /> Now, maybe in your game the Hollow Ones didn't betray the Traditions. In that case they might be a better group of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s nothing wrong with Romanticism. And I didn\u2019t know the Hollow Ones betrayed the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T00:11:11-08:00","id":1527990,"title":"","content":"It depends on WHICH Technocracy because every Technocracy in every Edition is utterly irreconcilable.<br /> <br /> I have had people literally argue the Technocracy is a bunch of progressives out to save human society and bring equality to all people versus the terrorist racist Traditions when they are based on the forces of Western capitalism hegemony versus a bunch of oppressed colonized peoples.<br /> <br /> And you know what? THAT IS BACKED UP BY SOME EDITIONS.<br /> <br /> M5's biggest challenge will be settling the debate once and for all whether the Union is the science faction, a bunch of fascists, or somehow this bizarre fascist progressive movement that has no relationship to real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-05-2024, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T01:58:06-08:00","id":1528001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1527990#post1527990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M5's biggest challenge will be settling the debate once and for all whether the Union is the science fiction, a bunch of fascists, or somehow this bizarre fascist progressive movement that has no relationship to real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>As with most things in the WOD, I think the Union has all of that, between individuals and factions. And so do the Traditions. Ideologically monolithic entities are rare.<br /> In a contemporary setting, I play Union members mostly as tech-bros who have an idealistic vision but are too narrow-sighted to the consequences of their actions. They enthusiastically let genies out of their bottles without thinking it through. Of course, there is always room for some straight villain if the script demands it.<br /> <br /> The bigger clash for me is thematic - is a Solarpunk ending really something that fits into a WOD setting? To be fair, Mage is probably the only splat where I wouldn't categorically say &quot;no&quot;. Expanding the Ascension theme to the wider society isn't <i>too</i> far of a leap.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T03:47:52-08:00","id":1528005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1527975#post1527975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There\u2019s nothing wrong with Romanticism. And I didn\u2019t know the Hollow Ones betrayed the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>In several storylines the Hollow Ones help the Technocracy to destroy the central Tradition Horizon Realm. This causes the death and enslavement of thousands of Mages, family members, friends, and allies. So there is bad blood.<br /> <br /> The kind of Romanticism the Hollow Ones that betrayed the Trads go in for sacrifices everything for the Romantic's inner storyline. Toss in the old &quot;<b>Terror Virtue</b>&quot; ideology that Maximilian Robespierre championed and Stalin, Hitler, and Mao, all embraced, and Romanticism can get brutal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-05-2024, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T04:27:47-08:00","id":1528006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528005#post1528005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In several storylines the Hollow Ones help the Technocracy to destroy the central Tradition Horizon Realm. This causes the death and enslavement of thousands of Mages, family members, friends, and allies. So there is bad blood.<br /> <br /> The kind of Romanticism the Hollow Ones that betrayed the Trads go in for sacrifices everything for the Romantic's inner storyline. Toss in the old &quot;<b>Terror Virtue</b>&quot; ideology that Maximilian Robespierre championed and Stalin, Hitler, and Mao, all embraced, and Romanticism can get brutal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean there's the argument this is in character for them or the argument this is Character AssassinationTM of the highest order.<br /> <br /> Because when I think of Goths, I think of people who side with the conservative totalitarians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T04:30:53-08:00","id":1528007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528001#post1528001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with most things in the WOD, I think the Union has all of that, between individuals and factions. And so do the Traditions. Ideologically monolithic entities are rare.<br /> In a contemporary setting, I play Union members mostly as tech-bros who have an idealistic vision but are too narrow-sighted to the consequences of their actions. They enthusiastically let genies out of their bottles without thinking it through. Of course, there is always room for some straight villain if the script demands it.<br /> <br /> The bigger clash for me is thematic - is a Solarpunk ending really something that fits into a WOD setting? To be fair, Mage is probably the only splat where I wouldn't categorically say &quot;no&quot;. Expanding the Ascension theme to the wider society isn't <i>too</i> far of a leap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without getting into the complicated history of mage and the retcons behind the Union, I'm inclined to think that the version taken by M20 was the rare case of OPP making a mistake. We live in a time period with a lot of oppressive power structures that have caused massive societal upheaval and distress. They're motivated by greed, traditionalism, and control. They start wars and have unlimited funding.<br /> <br /> Basically, if the Union existed it would have to be closer to the Seers of the Throne or have no power whatsoever, at least to the extent of being reality police.<br /> <br /> So if they do revise the Technocracy in M5, I think they should probably have the Nephandi fully corrupt them and the survivors forced to join the Traditionalists. Maybe sand off the rough edges of both groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T05:35:14-08:00","id":1528014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1527990#post1527990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M5's biggest challenge will be settling the debate once and for all whether the Union is the science faction, a bunch of fascists, or somehow this bizarre fascist progressive movement that has no relationship to real life.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528006#post1528006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because when I think of Goths, I think of people who side with the conservative totalitarians.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528007#post1528007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if they do revise the Technocracy in M5, I think they should probably have the Nephandi fully corrupt them and the survivors forced to join the Traditionalists. Maybe sand off the rough edges of both groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, on the other hand, hope that they <i>don't</i> try to turn the Technocracy into cardboard cutout stand-ins for the \u201ceeevyl conservatives\u201d. I <i>prefer</i> it when Mage leaves it up to the Storyteller to decide, and doesn't try to force a particular interpretation down your throat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CT Phipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528007#post1528007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without getting into the complicated history of mage and the retcons behind the Union, I'm inclined to think that the version taken by M20 was the rare case of OPP making a mistake. We live in a time period with a lot of oppressive power structures that have caused massive societal upheaval and distress. They're motivated by greed, traditionalism, and control. They start wars and have unlimited funding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree with this, save only that the motivations aren't really traditionalism; they tend to be more along the lines of the \u201cbizarre fascist progressive movement\u201d that you claim has no relationship to real life.<br /> <br /> As villains, the Technocracy isn't specifically right-wing <i>or</i> left-wing; it's \u201cI know what's best for you, and can run your life better than you\u201d. As <i>heroes, </i>it actually has some evidence suggesting that this might be <i>true</i> to an extent.<br /> <br /> But again, I don't think that it's Mage's job to \u201csettle the debate\u201d. Mage is at its best when it's <i>facilitating</i> debates, not ending them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-05-2024, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T06:22:20-08:00","id":1528017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b