 life better than you\u201d. As <i>heroes, </i>it actually has some evidence suggesting that this might be <i>true</i> to an extent.<br /> <br /> But again, I don't think that it's Mage's job to \u201csettle the debate\u201d. Mage is at its best when it's <i>facilitating</i> debates, not ending them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T06:25:47-08:00","id":1528018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528006#post1528006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean there's the argument this is in character for them or the argument this is Character AssassinationTM of the highest order.<br /> <br /> Because when I think of Goths, I think of people who side with the conservative totalitarians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hollow Ones aren't identical to Goths. Remember, they are now the <b><i>Right and Romance </i></b>crowd. Leninism (it doesn't much resemble anything Marx wrote) and Fascism are both &quot;Romantic&quot; movements. Remember I specified that there are plenty of honorable Hollow Ones, they weren't trying to help the Technocracy destroy a Tradition stronghold with the full knowledge that it would lead to the death or enslavement of the population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T06:53:42-08:00","id":1528020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528007#post1528007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without getting into the complicated history of mage and the retcons behind the Union, I'm inclined to think that the version taken by M20 was the rare case of OPP making a mistake. We live in a time period with a lot of oppressive power structures that have caused massive societal upheaval and distress. They're motivated by greed, traditionalism, and control. They start wars and have unlimited funding.<br /> <br /> Basically, if the Union existed it would have to be closer to the Seers of the Throne or have no power whatsoever, at least to the extent of being reality police.<br /> <br /> So if they do revise the Technocracy in M5, I think they should probably have the Nephandi fully corrupt them and the survivors forced to join the Traditionalists. Maybe sand off the rough edges of both groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly sounds like the kind of thing that a 5th edition would do. It uproots major elements of the game and eliminates much of the original character as well as any possible nuance. I don't think its a good idea at all.<br /> <br /> Even if you compare the Technocracy at their worst to the Nephandi, the two are <i>very</i> different kinds of corruption. The Technocracy embodies the corruption of power, noble cause corruption, and systemic corruption. They don't need an outside influence to become manipulative and oppressive tyrants; personal greed, lack of transparency, and an unexamined sense of righteousness are all it takes.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi are about metaphysical and existential corruption and destruction. They're not the Seers, they are the Scelesti. They can't take the same place as the Technocracy because they're not coherent enough, nor do they desire to rule or maintain. If they did take the place of the Technocracy, they would use that position to destroy everything or they would rapidly crumble and fall out of power. That's an interesting idea for a chronicle, but not for the baseline of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T07:02:35-08:00","id":1528021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528020#post1528020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That certainly sounds like the kind of thing that a 5th edition would do. It uproots major elements of the game and eliminates much of the original character as well as any possible nuance. I don't think its a good idea at all.<br /> <br /> Even if you compare the Technocracy at their worst to the Nephandi, the two are <i>very</i> different kinds of corruption. The Technocracy embodies the corruption of power, noble cause corruption, and systemic corruption. They don't need an outside influence to become manipulative and oppressive tyrants; personal greed, lack of transparency, and an unexamined sense of righteousness are all it takes.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi are about metaphysical and existential corruption and destruction. They're not the Seers, they are the Scelesti. They can't take the same place as the Technocracy because they're not coherent enough, nor do they desire to rule or maintain. If they did take the place of the Technocracy, they would use that position to destroy everything or they would rapidly crumble and fall out of power. That's an interesting idea for a chronicle, but not for the baseline of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right the nephandi are a poor fit.<br /> <br /> But I do think in this time of rising authoritanism, crushing local cultures under capitalist imperialism, and post-truth agendas that it may be a time to revisit the Union and think the M20 idea of them being misguided idealists was...naive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T07:53:12-08:00","id":1528023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528021#post1528021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I do think in this time of rising authoritanism, crushing local cultures under capitalist imperialism, and post-truth agendas that it may be a time to revisit the Union and think the M20 idea of them being misguided idealists was...naive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree, but I also don't think they would need a heavy-handed type cast. You can still have a Union where the more radical elements have the upper hand, but with others whose road to hell is paved with good intentions still present. Losing the internal complexity would make the Technocracy less interesting, imo, I much prefer their diversified ideals to what essentially would be a faction of Weaver Drones- to put it another way, antagonists whose agenda has <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heartbreaking:_The_Worst_Person_You_Know_Just_Made_A_Great_Point\" target=\"_blank\">relatable</a> elements makes them more engaging for players to reflect on those points. It invites discourse, which I consider a main benefit of playing Mage (and most other WOD games). If you're worried that the significance of the destructive and corrupting elements of the faction are watered down that way, I would say that pure villains are actually worse for that: the good vs evil narrative is something authoritarian structures love to push because it keeps people from thinking too hard about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 01-05-2024, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T08:35:29-08:00","id":1528026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1527990#post1527990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M5's biggest challenge will be settling the debate once and for all whether the Union is the science faction, a bunch of fascists, or somehow this bizarre fascist progressive movement that has no relationship to real life.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528006#post1528006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because when I think of Goths, I think of people who side with the conservative totalitarians.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528007#post1528007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if they do revise the Technocracy in M5, I think they should probably have the Nephandi fully corrupt them and the survivors forced to join the Traditionalists. Maybe sand off the rough edges of both groups.</div> </div> </div> </div> I, on the other hand, hope that they don't try to turn the Technocracy into cardboard cutout stand-ins for the \u201ceeevyl conservatives\u201d. I prefer it when Mage leaves it up to the Storyteller to decide, and doesn't try to force a particular interpretation down your throat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CT Phipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528007#post1528007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without getting into the complicated history of mage and the retcons behind the Union, I'm inclined to think that the version taken by M20 was the rare case of OPP making a mistake. We live in a time period with a lot of oppressive power structures that have caused massive societal upheaval and distress. They're motivated by greed, traditionalism, and control. They start wars and have unlimited funding.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mostly agree with this, save only that the motivations aren't really traditionalism; they tend to be more along the lines of the \u201cbizarre fascist progressive movement\u201d that you claim has no relationship to real life.<br /> <br /> As villains, the Technocracy isn't specifically right-wing or left-wing; it's \u201cI know what's best for you, and can run your life better than you\u201d. As heroes, it actually has some evidence suggesting that this might be true to an extent.<br /> <br /> But again, I don't think that it's Mage's job to \u201csettle the debate\u201d. Mage is at its best when it's facilitating debates, not ending them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T08:58:46-08:00","id":1528027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1527854#post1527854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see the Traditions win, but I also wouldn\u2019t mind a future in which the Technocracy and the Traditions work together for the greater good of humanity. In terms of generations, I was born into Gen X, but I definitely don\u2019t think like them. I\u2019m much more like a Millennial or even Gen Z (the term Artist Generation for Gen Z really resonates with me).</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, no matter which generation\u2019s values it reflects, I would like to see a generally hopeful and optimistic take on Mage when they do the next edition, in stark contrast to the very downbeat take on Vampire in V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T14:02:39-08:00","id":1528167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528018#post1528018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hollow Ones aren't identical to Goths. Remember, they are now the <b><i>Right and Romance </i></b>crowd. Leninism (it doesn't much resemble anything Marx wrote) and Fascism are both &quot;Romantic&quot; movements. Remember I specified that there are plenty of honorable Hollow Ones, they weren't trying to help the Technocracy destroy a Tradition stronghold with the full knowledge that it would lead to the death or enslavement of the population.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Goths aren't usually hunted down by fascist authoritarian paramilitary groups. Which the Hollow Ones are.<br /> <br /> So this is collaboration as a persecuted minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T15:18:16-08:00","id":1528227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528167#post1528167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but Goths aren't usually hunted down by fascist authoritarian paramilitary groups. Which the Hollow Ones are.<br /> <br /> So this is collaboration as a persecuted minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>The World of Darkness - Austin Powers crossover we all needed, with Frau Farbissina as founder of the militant wing of the Salvation Army under the Technocracy/Second Inquisition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T16:19:30-08:00","id":1528229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1528227#post1528227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The World of Darkness - Austin Powers crossover we all needed, with Frau Farbissina as founder of the militant wing of the Salvation Army under the Technocracy/Second Inquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many films could be made this way? And better yet, why am I laughing at this idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T08:27:14-07:00","id":1532327,"title":"","content":"So, as a few discussions about the Union have been popping up, I decided to give another spin in this topic.<br /> <br /> I think I already suggested this previously, but we could have a less &quot;open war&quot; between Trads and Union, upon which it is clear that a somewhat reformed Union has won, but now their job is to &quot;occupy the enemy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thus yes, they more or less &quot;join forces&quot;.<br /> <br /> The way I envision it is with some changes at the &quot;Time Table&quot;, with the Union making concessions to the Trads - things like &quot;Feng Shui&quot; or &quot;Herbs Medicine&quot; and Meditation.<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, this would make the world of Mage become MORE like the real world instead of &quot;unleash the powah of Sciencaaaaaaaaaa!&quot;. Because let's be honest here, we have millions of people who abhor vaccines, who believe in angels and demons and curses and even people who believe that the Earth is flat.<br /> <br /> We also have many pseudoscience esoterica about &quot;quantum energy&quot; nonsense, and we always find women debating about the importance of their birth signal and what Mars being ascendant in Venus means for their prospects on a date or job interview.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, statistical data performed under rigorous methodologies is used or tossed aside according to the individuals' preconceived beliefs, which range from believing in Reincarnation of the spirit to the staunch materialist atheists like myself.<br /> <br /> So, a world upon which there's a reason why humanity still holds to those mystical and pseudoscientific beliefs instead of skeptical materialist atheism, it makes more sense for it to be a world upon which the rulers of it (the Techie boys) aren't &quot;Science Fascists&quot; - at least not in the &quot;Science&quot; part (they can still hold the &quot;Fascist&quot; portion thou).<br /> <br /> The problem would be were to divert conflict towards. If the Trads and Union get into a &quot;cease-fire&quot;, then the Trads main concern would be not to upset the Union too much, and the Union concern would be not to cause the Trads to get into open revolt.<br /> <br /> This scenario would be good if both factions get too weakened to deal with EXTERNAL treats on their own, and thus they get into an uneasy collaboration.<br /> <br /> Being how the Union likes to control, they could have an endless of bureocratic agreements with the Trads about &quot;sanctioned MagiK&quot;, and if a Mage infringes upon that, they could get a visit by the &quot;Federal Bureau of MagiK&quot; (MiB). But instead of sending them directly to Construct Mecha to be brainwashed or turned into drones, they get a &quot;fine&quot; or &quot;community service&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thus, once in a while a minor cancer can be cured by the &quot;power of faith&quot;, while you'll promptly have doctor's giving testimonies on the tabloids about the &quot;placebo effect&quot;, but in order to do so, first your Verbena has to get permission on Sector 7B of the bureau of &quot;Healing Activities&quot; and file this paper, then return to the office of &quot;Sanctioned Practices&quot; on the 13 floor for the 3 months of waiting process and then...<br /> <br /> So, this would bury things under some bizantine bureocracy, and things would be closely monitored and scrutinized at all times, which in my opinion gives an even better sense oppression to the Trads.<br /> <br /> So, each side gains something, but they also lose something in the process. The question that many would ask would be: is it worth it? Would you try to work within the system, or would you rebel and go rogue?<br /> <br /> Then, for the external treats, there would of course be the Nephandi and Marauders, the classic &quot;evil villain of the week&quot;, but also there would be &quot;Things-men-were-not-meant-to-know&quot;, but also there would be antagonism between Rogues from both sides - Disparates that were kept out of the deal and rogues from both the Technocracy, that refuse to accept those new terms and resort to &quot;techno-terrorism&quot; and Trads who refuse to follow the imposed rules; and besides those, there would also be traitors inside both ranks, who are displeased by these accomodations but who haven't yet being discovered and thus don't have a &quot;Wanted Dead or Alive&quot; sign post over their heads yet.<br /> <br /> And there would also be the more &quot;sociopathic&quot; elements on both sides trying to make a profit of the situation, those trying to simply climb the ladders of power without any concerns with idealistic ideas, and thus those individuals can cause great harm to this fragile balance.<br /> <br /> I gotta say, this would be very different, but it may be an interesting game to be played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 03-10-2024, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T07:21:12-07:00","id":1533746,"title":"","content":"As far as if it's desirable: No, from both an in-game and out-of-game standpoint. The Technocratic Union exemplifies all the harmful aspects of the Enlightenment and at its best written is a razor-sharp puncturing of the usual Western narratives around history and Progress (capital P intended). Unfortunately what they are often gets mistaken because people don't really understand the nature of the Union because the critique of those narratives is so foreign to them; this thread is an example. The Union is authoritarian and brutal, yes, but that actually has a long history in modernist political thought and is in part because of its rejection of traditionalism. If modernism is a belief in the ability of science and the state to remake society and nature in positive ways it follows that anyone getting in the way of that ought to be stopped with force.<br /> <br /> History makes this clear. Many of the science fiction utopias of old look utterly psychotic by today's standards. For one thing, they were horrifically racist; to quote one starry-eyed futurist's science fiction: &quot;In 'the survival of the fittest,' we English, along with the races kindred to us, have everywhere carried the day, and everywhere all others have been crowded off the world's too narrow surface.&quot; Rawson, in a book on the environmental imaginings of these utopians, tells us of &quot;[t]he naturalist William Delisle Hay [who] depicted the world's Anglo-Saxons assisting the process of evolution by annihilating the populations of Asia and Africa.&quot; They also happily concluded that the extinctions of other forms of life was simply Progress. In comparison, the often-maligned Romantics look quite sane by comparison. And while fascism is often attributed to Romanticism, the Nazis drew heavily from the medical establishment and Italian futurism, with its fetishization of the modern and speed, helped create fascism in the first place.<br /> <br /> I've always seen the Union as embodying the stuff that must be purged from science. Dropping their negative aspects has always felt like we're sweeping the extremely sordid history under the rug because, I don't know, we want to own the creationists or we're afraid someone will accuse us of being an anti-vaxxer. Especially when techno-fascism is rising again (see the longtermists) that won't do. So with that in mind, I'd have the Technocracy still be mages, still be horrific, and still be locked in battle with the Traditions and Crafts--but I'd create a Craft to fill their place. They'd be inherently unable to create anything magical (if you want to actually create magic nanotech goo and assemble an FTL drive out of spare parts, go play an Etherite), but would be able to incorporate magical materials into mundane technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","user":"Citrakayah","date":". 04-07-2024, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T08:21:05-07:00","id":1533750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1533746#post1533746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as if it's desirable: No, from both an in-game and out-of-game standpoint. The Technocratic Union exemplifies all the harmful aspects of the Enlightenment and at its best written is a razor-sharp puncturing of the usual Western narratives around history and Progress (capital P intended). Unfortunately what they are often gets mistaken because people don't really understand the nature of the Union because the critique of those narratives is so foreign to them; this thread is an example. The Union is authoritarian and brutal, yes, but that actually has a long history in modernist political thought and is in part because of its rejection of traditionalism. If modernism is a belief in the ability of science and the state to remake society and nature in positive ways it follows that anyone getting in the way of that ought to be stopped with force.<br /> <br /> History makes this clear. Many of the science fiction utopias of old look utterly psychotic by today's standards. For one thing, they were horrifically racist; to quote one starry-eyed futurist's science fiction: &quot;In 'the survival of the fittest,' we English, along with the races kindred to us, have everywhere carried the day, and everywhere all others have been crowded off the world's too narrow surface.&quot; Rawson, in a book on the environmental imaginings of these utopians, tells us of &quot;[t]he naturalist William Delisle Hay [who] depicted the world's Anglo-Saxons assisting the process of evolution by annihilating the populations of Asia and Africa.&quot; They also happily concluded that the extinctions of other forms of life was simply Progress. In comparison, the often-maligned Romantics look quite sane by comparison. And while fascism is often attributed to Romanticism, the Nazis drew heavily from the medical establishment and Italian futurism, with its fetishization of the modern and speed, helped create fascism in the first place.<br /> <br /> I've always seen the Union as embodying the stuff that must be purged from science. Dropping their negative aspects has always felt like we're sweeping the extremely sordid history under the rug because, I don't know, we want to own the creationists or we're afraid someone will accuse us of being an anti-vaxxer. Especially when techno-fascism is rising again (see the longtermists) that won't do. So with that in mind, I'd have the Technocracy still be mages, still be horrific, and still be locked in battle with the Traditions and Crafts--but I'd create a Craft to fill their place. They'd be inherently unable to create anything magical (if you want to actually create magic nanotech goo and assemble an FTL drive out of spare parts, go play an Etherite), but would be able to incorporate magical materials into mundane technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, those horrific ideas of Social Darwinism reinforced tribalistic dispositions, and tribalism is a characteristic that is evolutionaryly driven.<br /> <br /> In a very dark irony of history, the reason why we today are appalled by those ideas is because of the absolutely nightmarish hell that was WW1 but specially WW2. The 19th century was a time of euphoric and borderline psychotic optimism, upon which Western society was so sure that science would solve every single problem in the world, and not just social problems mind you, &quot;da Science&quot; would even fix every single MORAL problems too. It was the time of Julio Verne's science fiction novels and optimistic futurism.<br /> <br /> People also believed in eternal world peace, many times under a single (benevolent) world government.<br /> <br /> And all of those feverish dreams came crashing down under the horrors of the 2 world wars, that saw the &quot;wonders&quot; of science turned into nightmarish monstrosities.<br /> <br /> And we still live up to this day under the trauma of WW2. With the difference that now, it's no longer the proper trauma of it, but rather the trauma of being raised by generations who were traumatized by it and that spook us with their horror stories.<br /> <br /> But in a sense thou, we are beginning to look very much like the society of the end of the 19th century, with euphoric optimism and the same silly delusions about world peace.<br /> <br /> The one question I always had thou was: if there had been no world wars, would we still be as chauvinistic as we were in the 19th century? And I have to admit that the answer is &quot;probably yes_. So, the big irony is that the unimaginable evils of WW2 (in particular) forced us to become better. <br /> <br /> Every single one of us like to think that we are paragons of moral, but the truth is that, if we were Germans in the 1930's, we probably would be snitching our Jewish neighbors to the SS. We are not better because we are such great persons, we are better simply because we were born at the right time. Had we been born in Ancient Rome, we would be cheering and clapping at slaves killing each other at the arena, or we would say that what Rome needs is to crucify more people, because &quot;in the good old days there was no such leniency towards troublemakers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Modern society is entirely a byproduct of PTSD over the World Wars. Oh yes, and also the PTSD of imagining nuclear Armageddon on a daily basis over the Cold War. In a sense, the Western World is a traumatized society. But that is slowly fading away. WW2 will become &quot;ancient history&quot; - it's already beginning to show. And I'm not entirely sure that losing that trauma will be particularly good. Would we revert back to the natural state of tribalism once the memories of WW2 fade away? Who knows. Perhaps the fear of nuclear holocaust will keep us in line - but looking at how Russia and China have been behaving lately, perhaps even that won't be enough. And look how fast we forget about history - the first reaction towards Russian aggression was... Appeasement. 2008 Georgia, 2014 Crimea. And there are plenty of people that say we should just let them take Ukraine. &quot;Peace in our time&quot; comes to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T08:34:14-07:00","id":1533751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1533746#post1533746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always seen the Union as embodying the stuff that must be purged from science. Dropping their negative aspects has always felt like we're sweeping the extremely sordid history under the rug because, I don't know, we want to own the creationists or we're afraid someone will accuse us of being an anti-vaxxer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a right winger libertarian but... Yes. That's what drives me towards the Union. I have to admit it. I'm also a staunch atheist, and I cannot fathom superstitionist thinking being pushed. I... Actually never thought about that, but now that you mentioned, yes... This is true. Not that I'm afraid to be called an &quot;anti-vaccer&quot;, nor do I feel the need to &quot;own the creationists&quot; - well, except when they want to ban the teaching of Evolution and other such insanities. But I am a biologist, I see the world in an evolutionary manner, I always ponder which evolutionary processes could have rendered such and such behaviors, including in history and society. That's how my brain operates. Therefore I just simply cannot fathom the idea of advocating for astrology and faith healing. So, perhaps I might be a tiny little bit biased in this \ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> Sorry, it's always so funny to find out something about myself that I didn't previously know. I'm like a happy child right now upon such realization.<br /> <br /> Maybe I have been looking at the Union with pink glasses due to my love of &quot;da Science&quot;? Oh no no no, I do not want to have to deal with that.<br /> <br /> Union \u2764\ufe0f forever, don't make me change that \ud83d\ude2d<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T12:59:52-07:00","id":1533842,"title":"","content":"Speaking to the original question of the forum and giving it some thought, here are a couple of my own opinions, YMMV.<br /> <br /> I tend to be somewhat skeptical of the veracity of cycle-theories but I do such concepts to be interesting, at least on the level of inspiration or of creating certain categories for analyzing particular moments of history. I do however agree with the opening questions premise that the status of the society/culture which a game/work is produced in impacts that work; whether it is in alignment, opposition, or avoidant. Thus the question, would a status quo for Mage look different in the early-mid 2020s as opposed to the early-mid 1990s.<br /> <br /> Undoubtedly. While much of what makes the old WoD games great has a lasting appeal, they are also very clearly of certain cultural moments. Assuming that recognizable constituent parts remained in some form (Traditions, Union, etc.) but Mage started over it would certainly have differences in its outlook. Whether or not those differences would be more conducive to okay or storytelling comes down to a matter of preference.<br /> <br /> For me, I\u2019ve always been fond of the Cold War style Ascension War of early editions, where there are occasional flare ups of direct conflict but on earth most of the battle is sublimated into attempts alter consciousness in certain spheres of interest, with the umbra being grounds for a more open expression of conflict. Somewhat like the vibes you might get from Demon the Descent in Chronicles, as in both cases, whether Tradition Mage or Demon game, much depends on just how powerful and proactive the opposition forces are.<br /> <br /> That said, has the Technocracy won? In some ways yes. You could argue they had already won in 1e as well, thus was the cause for the scarcity of magick in the gothic-punk world of the Bush-Clinton 90s. However there are degrees to what \u2018winning\u2019 means. The revised shift, arguably, was less a matter of the final triumph of the TU and more a decision to foreclose on the possibility of the Ascension War being waged in earnest (outside maybe the Sphinx plot line stuff) as a scope of play. There\u2019s nothing wrong with that but whether you want to go that direction depends on the story you want to tell and the game you want to play.<br /> <br /> Even with a TU victory, there are still contradictions and cracks around the edges of things, just as there are in real life. The question then becomes how one wants to play in and characterize those contradictions, cracks, and fringes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T11:01:40-07:00","id":1549674,"title":"","content":"I find this discussion very interesting.<br /> <br /> Like many, I got into Mage and WoD when I was 12-14 years old, in this period that spans the late 90s and 2000s, and I agreee that there is a clear gen X mark on Mage, and this aspect got stale a long time ago.<br /> <br /> It's we the rag tag band of wiccans, artists and psychonauts vs the suits, vs the man, vs the matrix agents working in cubicle stations in their office towers. How silly this paradigm looks to us nowadays, specially when the crowd who plays tabletop RPGs became increasingly more homogenic, uniform and thin. At least werewolf has mythology and primaeval aesthetics to fall back into, when the eco warrior aspect seems silly. Mage has nothing.<br /> <br /> It's not by chance that the conversion of the technocracy to a more ambiguous or even positive faction happened together with the transition from gen X to millennials.<br /> <br /> What change will the transition to zoomers cause? Probably nephandi will be seen in a positive light and people will laugh about a game centered around reality consensus, where one of the factions is described as objectively and unambiguously evil not only by others but by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T12:50:07-07:00","id":1549675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1549674#post1549674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this discussion very interesting.<br /> <br /> Like many, I got into Mage and WoD when I was 12-14 years old, in this period that spans the late 90s and 2000s, and I agreee that there is a clear gen X mark on Mage, and this aspect got stale a long time ago.<br /> <br /> It's we the rag tag band of wiccans, artists and psychonauts vs the suits, vs the man, vs the matrix agents working in cubicle stations in their office towers. How silly this paradigm looks to us nowadays, specially when the crowd who plays tabletop RPGs became increasingly more homogenic, uniform and thin. At least werewolf has mythology and primaeval aesthetics to fall back into, when the eco warrior aspect seems silly. Mage has nothing.<br /> <br /> It's not by chance that the conversion of the technocracy to a more ambiguous or even positive faction happened together with the transition from gen X to millennials.<br /> <br /> What change will the transition to zoomers cause? Probably nephandi will be seen in a positive light and people will laugh about a game centered around reality consensus, where one of the factions is described as objectively and unambiguously evil not only by others but by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think this is true. A lot of new people, especially from Gen Z, are playing Dungeons and Dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T14:05:07-07:00","id":1549676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1549674#post1549674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when the eco warrior aspect seems silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It never is, and a whole lot of people in the US are poised to find out why with the administration's weakening of the Clean Water Act, among many other standards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T14:29:15-07:00","id":1549680,"title":"","content":"Pegging the evolution of the setting to social generations continues to be a questionable exercise even from the beginning of this thread.<br /> <br /> A bunch of young teenagers didn't knock on White Wolf's HQ's door (it had one back then!) to demand a more nuanced Technocracy. The people that made the games realized the overly simplistic &quot;good&quot; vs. &quot;evil&quot; setup in many 1e books doesn't suit the WoD the same way that complexity and a lack of simple answers does. VtM making the Sabbat playable being a success was far more influential to the Technocracy getting the treatment than Millennials getting old enough to play the games (since, you know, the first Sabbat PG came out in 1992, when the elder Millennials were still 11 or younger).<br /> <br /> I'd also love to see some support for the idea that TTRPG players have broadly become more homogenic instead of more diverse over time. A coalition of diverse groups - including ones that might normally consider themselves 'enemies' in chiller times - standing up to an even bigger threat is pretty resonant with the current cultural zeitgeist. A bunch of weirdos ganging together to resist the rise of an authoritarian regime is basically the ideal power fantasy for younger players right now; especially not anything like trying to rehabilitate the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T14:42:37-07:00","id":1549682,"title":"","content":"I strongly suspect that the only sensible answer to a somewhat -mischievous question is \u201cIt all depends on who the player characters side with and how well they roll.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T01:07:10-07:00","id":1549700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1549674#post1549674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this discussion very interesting.<br /> <br /> Like many, I got into Mage and WoD when I was 12-14 years old, in this period that spans the late 90s and 2000s, and I agreee that there is a clear gen X mark on Mage, and this aspect got stale a long time ago.<br /> <br /> It's we the rag tag band of wiccans, artists and psychonauts vs the suits, vs the man, vs the matrix agents working in cubicle stations in their office towers. How silly this paradigm looks to us nowadays, specially when the crowd who plays tabletop RPGs became increasingly more homogenic, uniform and thin. At least werewolf has mythology and primaeval aesthetics to fall back into, when the eco warrior aspect seems silly. Mage has nothing.<br /> <br /> It's not by chance that the conversion of the technocracy to a more ambiguous or even positive faction happened together with the transition from gen X to millennials.<br /> <br /> What change will the transition to zoomers cause? Probably nephandi will be seen in a positive light and people will laugh about a game centered around reality consensus, where one of the factions is described as objectively and unambiguously evil not only by others but by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Zoomers will prefer the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T01:16:38-07:00","id":1549702,"title":"","content":"Doomers and Zoomers aren't the same thing. Zoomers might understand why people fall into being Nephandi considering how bad Doomerism has become, but that's not the same thing.<br /> <br /> Can we stop shitting on an entire generation of young adults?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T14:48:37-07:00","id":1549718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1549702#post1549702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doomers and Zoomers aren't the same thing. Zoomers might understand why people fall into being Nephandi considering how bad Doomerism has become, but that's not the same thing.<br /> <br /> Can we stop shitting on an entire generation of young adults?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but every time I make a coherent fact based point with some Zoomer or Doomer I get &quot;Okay Boomer&quot; as a response. Could we stop sneering at people for being born before the Kennedy administration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T19:52:14-07:00","id":1549722,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Let's step away from intergenerational conflict, please. Ageism in any direction is not pertinent, nor is it welcome. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T23:50:03-07:00","id":1549724,"title":"","content":"Although the Technocoracy has its virtues they have two insurmountable faults. First, they are control freaks. They demand everybody do it their way. Control beyond function is destruction. Secondly the Technocoracy always thinks in terms of their preferred methodology. This inflexiblity brutally limits the functionality of the Technocoracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-05T18:08:53-07:00","id":1549854,"title":"","content":"The original take on the Technocracy was flawed for three reasons.<br /> <br /> First, the oversimplification was bad for the setting, period. WoD in general and Mage in particular, the game hurts with such a childish take on the many themes the Union represents.<br /> <br /> Second, and actually more important, both the Technocracy and the Traditions represent a lot of things, a huge lot of dualities and faux-dualities, and some of those were quite problematic to be in the box they were in.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Union is Imperialism, Control, Consumerism. They're also Science, Vaccines, the Common Good. The Traditions are Individualism, Self-Identity, but they're both the good and the bad of those things. They're strong proponents of the idea that some people are inherently better than others. Heck, most of the Nazi ideas would fit more in the Traditions than in the Union, specially their propaganda.<br /> <br /> Mashing all those things together and labeling them Good or Evil is very problematic in so many levels. And then we get the third problem: both are, at the end of the day, made up by people, and specially by Mages. One thing is to have the Traditions represent diversity and the Union represent uniformity. Another thing is to think this is effectively the only thing they have in their ranks. To think only the Traditions have enough diversity for individuals to improve above its flaws, while the Union is somehow as uniform as their facade shows.<br /> <br /> As is said in the GttT and in M20, at the end of the day they're Mages. The very definition of being an Awakened requires the agents of the Technocracy to be more than just cogs, regardless of how much they try to be (when they try to be). The idea that individuals within the Technocratic Union have different opinions about everything that's happening and everything they do, and try to improve, to do good from within a flawed system they think is good <i><b>despite</b></i> those flaws, they think can grow beyond those flaws with time, this idea is itself center to Mage, because it defines what being a Mage is about in the first place, regardless if you call yourself a Mage or not.<br /> <br /> Now, to say that players nowadays are more uniform is to just ignore how many people currently play RPGs and how diverse a background they have nowadays. Not only are more people playing, they're from more countries, more walks in life, more ethnic groups. And more of them get to participate in discussions through the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T22:09:08-07:00","id":1550471,"title":"","content":"It depends on what Technocracy you mean. Because I'm of the group that believes that there's really no way to reconcile the Technocracy of each edition and they're fundamentally reboots.<br /> <br /> Because it boils down to the question:<br /> <br /> &quot;Are the Technocrats fascists or socialists?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because they've been presented as both.<br /> <br /> Mage 1st Edition: The Pre-Victorian Technocrats were The Good Guy Order of Reason and became Fascists with the Technocracy. Genocide and Capitalism hoo rah!<br /> <br /> Mage 2nd Edition: The Guide to the Union made them well intentioned extremists.<br /> <br /> Mage 3rd Edition: The Technocracy has lost its leadership and are now collectivist socialists who for some reason don't respect human rights occasionally.<br /> <br /> Mage 20: They're actively good guys vs, a collectivist Umbral Technocracy.<br /> <br /> For me, I've come around to the fact that the Technocracy being fascists wasn't misrepresenting the people in power and the more punk I am, the more I think &quot;The Man&quot; should be pure evil and not ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Which is ironic because as a teenager, I used to think the Union was much more morally ambiguous but fit the World of Darkness better. Because the secret masters of the government is not a group that cares about humanity in this world or the next. If the Union actually did, it wouldn't be nearly as bad a world as it is in this world. You can't have the people in charge of a punk world be a bunch of caring idealists even if they are ruthless. They have to be scumbags because its not punk otherwise.<br /> <br /> It reminds me a bit of a RL conversation:<br /> <br /> &quot;I hate conspiracy theorists, it's all over the 90s World of Darkness. It's like 9/11 Truthers were right.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I mean, we also just lived through the President of the United States secretly arranging a coup attempt and that was after the Iraq War was under false pretenses.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, but those aren't conspiracy theories. They're fact. It's just journalism to expose them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I feel like we're talking past one another.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the end, pick any one of them because it's your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-29-2025, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T17:46:57-07:00","id":1550495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550471#post1550471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on what Technocracy you mean. Because I'm of the group that believes that there's really no way to reconcile the Technocracy of each edition and they're fundamentally reboots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; but no more so than the Traditions, who <i>also</i> have been reinvented in each edition. Which is part of the premise of this thread: times change, and so does the game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550471#post1550471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it boils down to the question:<br /> <br /> &quot;Are the Technocrats fascists or socialists?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because they've been presented as both.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two aren't mutually exclusive. And don't forget that the Union is composed of five Conventions which don't always see eye to eye. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550471#post1550471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage 1st Edition: The Pre-Victorian Technocrats were The Good Guy Order of Reason and became Fascists with the Technocracy. Genocide and Capitalism hoo rah!</div> </div> </div> </div> Mage 1st Edition didn't have much to say about the history of the Technocracy. Remember that the 1st Edition was only around for about a year before the 2nd edition came out; <i>most </i>of the game's development took place under the 2nd edition. And the Victorian Age didn't actually get explored until just a few years ago. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550471#post1550471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage 2nd Edition: The Guide to the Union made them well intentioned extremists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, the <b>Guide to the Technocracy</b> was one of the <i>last</i> books to come out under the 2nd edition, and the &quot;well intentioned extremists&quot; bit had its roots all the way back in the 1st edition: the Book of Shadows featured the notion of Technocrats as potential good guys, and it came out under the 1st edition of the game. If anything, the <b>Guide to the Technocracy</b> was a proto-Revised Edition book. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550471#post1550471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage 3rd Edition: The Technocracy has lost its leadership and are now collectivist socialists who for some reason don't respect human rights occasionally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping that you're not going by the Convention Books when you say this; because like <b>Guide to the Technocracy</b> came out just before Revised Edition, most of the Convention Books (all but <b>Iteration X</b>) came out just before <b>M20</b>. Check their copyright dates: they were published in 2012, just before development of <b>M20</b> started. I wouldn't call them proto-<b>M20</b> books, because the development team that created the Convention Books wasn't involved in creating <b>M20</b>; but they're <i>also</i> not <b>MRev</b> books in that they didn't come out until nearly eight years after the Revised edition had closed up shop. <br /> <br /> The developers of <b>MRev</b> saw the Technocracy as a cautionary tale for people who think that if you're an intellectual, you're immune to falling for toxic ideologies. Or at least highly resistant. Rather, the MRev Technocracy represents a trap into which intellectuals are particularly <i>prone</i> to falling. I got this directly from one of the writers for the Revised Edition, during the years when <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> was considered to be a dead game, before <b>V20</b> came along and relaunched the original World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550471#post1550471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage 20: They're actively good guys vs, a collectivist Umbral Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not <b>M20</b>'s Technocracy; that's <b>Void Engineers Convention Book</b>. Again, recall that it's a Union of five Conventions. The Convention Books highlighted those differences, with the Void Engineers being actively good guys (albeit militant ones) fighting to protect their Earthbound brothers from a collectivist Umbral Technocracy; the Syndicate was the capitalists; the NWO was the socialists; and the Progenitors were self-proclaimed healers trying to mend the rifts in the Union. But again, they're not really <b>\u200b\u200b\u200bM20</b>; although some ideas from there <i>did</i> find their way into <b>M20</b>. We didn't get a fleshed-out take on just what <b>M20</b>'s Technocracy is like until <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>; and even there, what we found out was that the Technocracy is whatever the Storyteller wants it to be. Which is a very <b>M20</b> thing to say, as the edition's mission statement was essentially &quot;it's your game; so with it as you will.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550471#post1550471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, I've come around to the fact that the Technocracy being fascists wasn't misrepresenting the people in power and the more punk I am, the more I think &quot;The Man&quot; should be pure evil and not ambiguous.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not Mage. With the sole exception of the Nephandi, Mage doesn't <i>\u200b\u200bdo</i> unambiguous. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550471#post1550471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is ironic because as a teenager, I used to think the Union was much more morally ambiguous but fit the World of Darkness better. Because the secret masters of the government is not a group that cares about humanity in this world or the next. If the Union actually did, it wouldn't be nearly as bad a world as it is in this world. You can't have the people in charge of a punk world be a bunch of caring idealists even if they are ruthless. They have to be scumbags because its not punk otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>But <i>should</i> <b>Mage</b> be punk? That's part of what it was in the 90s, true. But it's been over thirty years since then, and times have changed. <br /> <br /> At this stage, what I'd like to see for the Technocracy is an organization that's in the painful throes of reformation. Success isn't guaranteed by any means; but while Conditioning and Room 101 are still a thing, the Technocrats supporting it don't have the monopoly on power that they thought they had; the Friends of Courage can operate more or less openly now (whatever that means in the context of a secret society), and Technocrats who used to simply accept Room 101 as &quot;just how it is&quot; are starting to come around to the idea that the practice of brainwashing Technocrats into conformity is bad and ought to stop, regardless of the cost. Many may even be coming around to the idea that brainwashing <i>anyone </i>is problematic at best. <br /> <br /> That is, there <i>are</i> rotten Secret Masters running the Union; but the solution isn't to &quot;rage against the Man&quot; (the punk outlook); it's to <i>fix the Union. </i>And it's doable, albeit a tall order, because it's turning out that the seeming omnipotence of those Secret Masters was an illusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-29T22:18:13-07:00","id":1550501,"title":"","content":"It's also important to note that the Technocracy isn't <i>exactly</i> The Man.<br /> <br /> Sure, they're very much The Man from the POV of the Traditions, but that's in a context of war. And they're built as a parody of every conspiracy theory about a shadow government.<br /> <br /> But since very early it was made clear that the Union isn't really the shadow government. It tries to be, and it has a lot of influence, but there are other things out there, and in the end the Union is far from having absolute control over the big institutions.<br /> <br /> There <b>is</b> The Man in the setting, but it isn't <i>exactly</i> the Technocratic Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T03:48:39-07:00","id":1550505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550495#post1550495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But <i>should</i> <b>Mage</b> be punk? That's part of what it was in the 90s, true. But it's been over thirty years since then, and times have changed.<br /> <br /> At this stage, what I'd like to see for the Technocracy is an organization that's in the painful throes of reformation. Success isn't guaranteed by any means; but while Conditioning and Room 101 are still a thing, the Technocrats supporting it don't have the monopoly on power that they thought they had; the Friends of Courage can operate more or less openly now (whatever that means in the context of a secret society), and Technocrats who used to simply accept Room 101 as &quot;just how it is&quot; are starting to come around to the idea that the practice of brainwashing Technocrats into conformity is bad and ought to stop, regardless of the cost. Many may even be coming around to the idea that brainwashing <i>anyone </i>is problematic at best.<br /> <br /> That is, there <i>are</i> rotten Secret Masters running the Union; but the solution isn't to &quot;rage against the Man&quot; (the punk outlook); it's to <i>fix the Union. </i>And it's doable, albeit a tall order, because it's turning out that the seeming omnipotence of those Secret Masters was an illusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion on the specifics of the Union is that I don't really have any specifics on the Union anymore so I'm not really capable of commenting on the rest of the post but this part is one I do have strong have opinions on. I think Mage actually kind of suffers and benefits from the fact that it is a game where the nature of virtually every faction has been rewritten and done ambiguously enough that the biggest struggle of any ST is picking a lane as to what is true or not.<br /> <br /> But is Mage punk?<br /> <br /> I'd argue Mage is actually the MOST punk of the &quot;Big Three&quot; gamelines and that Revised was correct in retrospect that there needed to be a serious course correction from the guys who were die-hard Traditionalist and die-hard Unionist apologists. Because Vampire: The Masquerade and Werewolf: The Apocalypse kind of got themselves caught in the weeds. In V:TM, the anarchs became just as bad as the Camarilla or worse because they were less sexy and cool while the Sabbat became the only opposition anyone took seriously despite being a bunch of meathead religious fanatics. Werewolf also got caught up in the Garou Nation's flaws before 5th Edition exaggerated them to the point of ridiculousness.<br /> <br /> Mage by contrast has always been the only game where they kept the central premise of organizing your protagonists and disparate viewpoint about fixing the world or standing in opposition to the fucked up nature of the world. In a very real way, both VTM and WTA lost that somewhere along the way.<br /> <br /> I kind of think back to the Mage's inspirations whenever I'm thinking of this. Grant Morrison's INVISIBLES for example. At some point, the ideal Mage character went from being a Hollow One and his cabal of disparate friends versus the Union and became ideologically committed Order of Hermes or Unionists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T03:56:30-07:00","id":1550506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550501#post1550501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also important to note that the Technocracy isn't <i>exactly</i> The Man.<br /> <br /> Sure, they're very much The Man from the POV of the Traditions, but that's in a context of war. And they're built as a parody of every conspiracy theory about a shadow government.<br /> <br /> But since very early it was made clear that the Union isn't really the shadow government. It tries to be, and it has a lot of influence, but there are other things out there, and in the end the Union is far from having absolute control over the big institutions.<br /> <br /> There <b>is</b> The Man in the setting, but it isn't <i>exactly</i> the Technocratic Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is, IMHO, a rabbit hole and a beautiful rabbit hole.<br /> <br /> I do think that the game invited its audience to question everything and that resulted in the humanization of the Union and their perspective. But I also feel like it's a gameline that requires an antagonist at the wheel of reality that is fundamentally wrong. Chronicles of Darkness made the metaphor literal by creating the Seers of the Throne as the Matrix's Machines. They're the Gnostic Demiurge's minions and the people keeping everyone else asleep.<br /> <br /> And the motive of the Seers is, &quot;Fuck you, I've got mine.&quot;<br /> <br /> Morally indefensible.<br /> <br /> The Union isn't that because it wants to wake up humanity as well and has a point. Which you might argue is much better. However, we're kind of in a society today where there is in fact a huge chunk of society that aggressively wants to keep people ignorant, stupid, poor, and an underclass. They never were NOT there. As you say, there is absolutely The ManTM in Mage because the ManTM exists in RL. People who are basically Pentex, that much-maligned bunch of cartoon villains.<br /> <br /> A flaw of Mage is that unless you make the Nephandi a massive group, Mage suffers from being too idealistic for its own good. There's no group that fundamentally does hold the keys to humanity's ignorance and supports keeping them jailed because at their worst, the Union is idealistic just like the Traditions.<br /> <br /> And humanity has shown there is a massive chunk who are anti-idealists. There needs to be a Seers, Pentex, or even Camarilla motivated by keeping mankind under the thumb. The Union outgrew that rule or never fit it properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T04:25:15-07:00","id":1550507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550505#post1550505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of think back to the Mage's inspirations whenever I'm thinking of this. Grant Morrison's INVISIBLES for example. At some point, the ideal Mage character went from being a Hollow One and his cabal of disparate friends versus the Union and became ideologically committed Order of Hermes or Unionists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just the opposite, actually. <br /> <br /> One of the innovations of <b>M20</b> that's often overlooked is that it broke the stranglehold that the Traditions, Conventions, and Crafts had on paradigm in earlier editions of the game. That is, it <i>used to be</i> that if you wanted to play a Martial Artist, you did so by picking the Akashic Brotherhood as your Tradition, and it supplied the Theory/ Philosophy and Practice. In <b>M20</b>, the new Focus rules makes that sort of thing a fundamentally personal and individualistic choice; and the choice of which group you subscribe to is now almost an afterthought, something that can be completely skipped without harm to the character. As such, the game is actually much more adept at facilitating the &quot;Hollow One and his cabal of disparate friends&quot; style of gaming, whereas the &quot;ideologically committed Order of Hermes or Unionists&quot; are largely holdovers from previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T10:38:57-07:00","id":1550745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1549674#post1549674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's we the rag tag band of wiccans, artists and psychonauts vs the suits, vs the man, vs the matrix agents working in cubicle stations in their office towers. How silly this paradigm looks to us nowadays, specially when the crowd who plays tabletop RPGs became increasingly more homogenic, uniform and thin. At least werewolf has mythology and primaeval aesthetics to fall back into, when the eco warrior aspect seems silly. Mage has nothing.<br /> <br /> It's not by chance that the conversion of the technocracy to a more ambiguous or even positive faction happened together with the transition from gen X to millennials.<br /> <br /> What change will the transition to zoomers cause? Probably nephandi will be seen in a positive light and people will laugh about a game centered around reality consensus, where one of the factions is described as objectively and unambiguously evil not only by others but by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a Zoomer WoD (especially Mage) fan, I don't see Nephandi in a positive light, and I am very anti-Technocracy. I was going through puberty when the Snowden leaks happened, and I was pissed. Then, a few years later, I got epilepsy, and started being pissed with big pharma. And then there's the whole &quot;NWO supported Nazis and uses Jews as scapegoats&quot; thing. I was raised on &quot;The Matrix,&quot; so maybe that's part of why fighting evil Agents doesn't feel so weird to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T12:48:16-07:00","id":1550755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522398-should-the-technocracy-win?p=1550745#post1550745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking as a Zoomer WoD (especially Mage) fan, I don't see Nephandi in a positive light, and I am very anti-Technocracy. I was going through puberty when the Snowden leaks happened, and I was pissed. Then, a few years later, I got epilepsy, and started being pissed with big pharma. And then there's the whole &quot;NWO supported Nazis and uses Jews as scapegoats&quot; thing. I was raised on &quot;The Matrix,&quot; so maybe that's part of why fighting evil Agents doesn't feel so weird to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Technocracy's biggest problem is that it has a huge playability factor that rivals the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Being a bunch of secret agents and cyborgs fighting wizards is, in fact, incredibly cool.<br /> <br /> The fact that they're the bad guys doesn't really resonate in a gameline devoted to playing bad guys. You know, what with V:TM being the big brother that takes everyone else's lunch money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T13:25:25-07:00","id":1550758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/